window.LUNA_CHAPTERS=(window.LUNA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":201,"title":"Chapter 201 Jealous Alpha","paragraphs":["Logan caught the change in Lainey at once. It wasn’t Alpha Killian choosing Eira that had shaken her. It was learning that Eira was an orphan.","He had noticed the resemblance earlier. Something in Eira’s features reminded him of Henry Crawford.","But Vincent, Henry’s own son, had shown no sign of recognition, so Logan had dismissed it as a coincidence.","Now he wasn’t so sure.","After Vincent disappeared through airport security, Logan turned to Lainey.","\"You noticed it too, didn’t you?\"","Her pulse jumped. \"Noticed what?\"","\"Eira looks like someone.\"","Lainey held his gaze. \"Who?\"","Logan almost said Henry. Then common sense kicked in. Suggesting that a prominent Alpha might have a daughter no one knew about was a good way to get himself blacklisted by half the Packs on the East Coast.","\"I can’t place it,\" he said. \"Probably just one of those faces.\"","\"Probably.\"","Neither of them believed that.","As they headed toward the parking garage, Lainey pulled out her phone.","She needed to look into Eira’s past before anyone else connected the dots.","--","Upstairs, Eira ordered roast chicken, braised short ribs, seasonal vegetables, and enough sides for the table. She also asked the server to bring out whatever was ready first.","Lila glanced around the private dining room. \"How did you find this place?\"","\"We had Dr. Shaw’s birthday dinner here. The food’s good, and Miles has been living on airport snacks and takeout for days.\"","Miles placed a hand over his heart. \"Someone finally sees me.\"","Alpha Killian gave him a cool look.","\"Still worth it,\" Miles said. \"I can’t eat another airport sandwich.\"","Eira smiled. \"You earned a real meal.\"","\"I was only doing what Alpha Killian asked.\"","\"I know.\" Her eyes shifted to Alpha Killian. \"I owe him too.\"","Alpha Killian held her gaze for a moment. Something warm and possessive flickered in his silver-gray eyes before he reached for his water.","The first dishes arrived, filling the room with the smell of rosemary, roasted garlic, and warm sourdough. Once everyone had food, Susan returned to business.","\"Vincent and Fiona recognized me downstairs,\" Susan said. \"They’ll probably figure out you’re going after the money.\"","Eira cut into her chicken. \"That’s fine. Sebastian knows I want a full accounting. He just doesn’t think I can prove anything.\"","Lila looked up from her mashed potatoes. \"Can Serena still claim the money was for research?\"","\"She can try,\" Susan said. \"But the records tell a different story. If she used fake invoices to cover personal spending, she may have a fraud problem too.\"","Lila raised her hand across the table. Eira laughed and gave her a quick high five.","Alpha Killian quietly poured her a bowl of chicken soup and slid it across the table.","\"Thanks.\" Eira smiled at him.","The sight caught him off guard.","When Alpha Killian had first met Eira, she had been crying. After that, she had kept everyone at a careful distance. She had spent years as a lone Omega without a wolf or a Pack to protect her, and that caution had become second nature.","It had taken months for her to smile this easily around him.","Sebastian had once seen that smile every day.","The thought left a bitter taste in Alpha Killian’s mouth. He drained his water.","Lila caught him reaching for the bottle again. \"Are you planning to leave any water for the rest of us?\"","Alpha Killian ignored her.","\"The food isn’t that salty,\" Eira said.","Miles lowered his eyes to hide a smile. Susan suddenly became very interested in her wine.","Alpha Killian pushed the soup closer to Eira. \"Eat before it gets cold.\"","She took a sip, and the warm broth finally brought back her appetite.","--","After dinner, Alpha Killian turned to Miles. \"Take the next three days off. Put them down as comp time.\"","Miles grinned. \"Thanks, Alpha. I’ll try not to check my email.\"","\"Don’t try. Just stay offline.\"","Susan and Miles left together. The moment they were gone, Lila linked her arm through Eira’s.","\"Sleepover at Number Nine?\"","\"Sure.\"","\"Perfect.\" Lila started pulling her toward the parking lot.","\"Eira.\"","Alpha Killian’s voice stopped them.","She looked back.","\"I’ll drive you home,\" he said, nodding toward his SUV.","\"I came with Lila.\"","\"And she can ride with us.\"","Lila gave him a knowing look. \"Smooth.\"","\"What about your Mustang?\" Eira asked.","Alpha Killian held out his hand. \"Keys. One of my security guys will bring it over.\"","Lila stared at him. \"And who’s driving us?\"","\"I am.\"","Her eyebrows shot up. \"Killian Sterling is driving me home himself? Should I take a picture, or will that hurt your brand?\"","\"Keys, Lila.\"","Laughing, she dropped them into his palm. Alpha Killian passed them to one of the Pack security officers waiting near the entrance.","He got behind the wheel. Eira took the passenger seat, and Lila climbed into the back.","As Eira buckled up, Lila leaned between the front seats.","\"We should stop for ice cream. Then we can put on that true-crime series when we get home.\"","Alpha Killian caught the shoulder of her leather jacket and eased her back.","\"Seat belt.\"","Lila dropped into her seat with a huff. \"You know, normal people say please.\"","\"Normal people don’t crawl into the front seat.\"","\"We’re still parked.\"","Alpha Killian started the engine. \"Not anymore.\"","Lila buckled up, caught Eira’s eye in the rearview mirror, and mouthed, Control freak.","Eira pressed her lips together to hide a laugh.","Alpha Killian had not even won her over yet, and he was already guarding the passenger seat like contested Pack territory.","If they ever became mates, Lila suspected every unmated wolf in California would need security clearance just to say hello."]},{"number":202,"title":"Chapter 202 A Broom and a Grudge","paragraphs":["The SUV pulled up in front of Number Nine.","Mrs. Jones stood on the porch with her phone in one hand and the two German shepherds at her side. Both dogs were still staring at the driveway, alert and restless.","Her expression softened when Eira and Lila climbed out.","\"There you are. I was starting to worry.\"","Then Alpha Killian stepped out from behind the wheel.","Mrs. Jones blinked. \"Alpha Killian. This is a surprise.\"","\"Good or bad?\"","\"The jury’s still out.\"","Eira smiled and crouched to greet the dogs. Both shepherds crowded around her, tails thumping against the porch.","\"What happened here?\"","\"Margaret Hale happened.\" Mrs. Jones planted the broom against the railing. \"She came over demanding that you talk her son into eating.\"","Eira glanced at the dogs. \"Did she leave quietly?\"","\"That’s what she says. Apparently, he won’t touch his food, and somehow that’s Miss Eira’s problem.\"","\"It isn’t,\" Alpha Killian said.","Mrs. Jones gave him an approving nod. \"Exactly what I told her. Well, my version had a few more words in it.\"","Eira glanced at the broom. \"And that came into it how?\"","\"Margaret wouldn’t leave. She started yelling, the dogs didn’t like her tone, and things got a little lively.\"","A strip of camel-colored wool clung to one shepherd’s collar.","Eira pulled it free. \"Is this from her coat?\"","\"Just the hem,\" Mrs. Jones said. \"Nobody bit her.\"","\"Good.\" Alpha Killian glanced at the dogs. \"A bite would mean lawyers and animal control.\"","Mrs. Jones snorted. \"That woman had it coming.\"","\"Maybe, but let’s stick to barking next time.\" Eira scratched both dogs behind the ears. \"Designer wool isn’t good for you.\"","They gazed up at her with matching looks of innocence.","As they went inside, Mrs. Jones lowered her voice. \"I don’t like the Hales knowing where you’re staying. Margaret came alone tonight. Next time, she might bring the whole family.\"","\"The work at Ten Ashford Lane is almost finished,\" Eira said. \"We’re waiting on the security system. Mrs. Jones and I can move in once it passes inspection.\"","Alpha Killian had known about the house, but he had never seen it.","\"What kind of security are you installing?\"","\"Cameras, motion sensors, reinforced locks, and a monitored alarm. Professor Davies recommended the contractor.\"","\"And the property?\"","\"Fourteen hundred square feet. Two bedrooms, two bathrooms, and a home office. It’s in a quiet neighborhood.\"","Alpha Killian frowned. \"Fourteen hundred?\"","Eira hung her coat by the door. \"It’s plenty for two people.\"","\"Two?\" Alpha Killian and Lila asked at the same time.","Mrs. Jones laughed. \"Relax. She means me.\"","Lila stared at her. \"You’re moving in too?\"","\"Someone has to keep Miss Eira fed and keep the Hales off the porch.\"","\"What about me?\"","\"You can stay whenever you want,\" Eira said.","Mrs. Jones smiled. \"You two can share the primary bedroom.\"","Lila brightened immediately. \"Even better.\"","She shot Alpha Killian a victorious look. She had a standing invitation and a spot in Eira’s bed. He did not even have a key.","Alpha Killian read every smug thought on her face.","\"Fair warning,\" he told Eira. \"Lila steals the blankets.\"","\"I do not.\"","\"She also kicks in her sleep.\"","\"You’re making that up.\"","\"And she snores.\"","Lila stared at him. \"Wow. This from the guy who growls in his sleep.\"","Alpha Killian’s eyes narrowed. \"I don’t growl.\"","\"You absolutely do. The whole west wing used to hear you.\"","Eira covered a laugh with her hand.","Alpha Killian looked at her. \"Don’t encourage her.\"","That only made her laugh harder.","Lila grabbed a throw pillow and fired it at him. Alpha Killian caught it without looking.","Their voices filled the living room, easy and ridiculous. Once, that kind of noise would have worn Eira out.","Tonight, it made Number Nine feel like a home.","--","Southridge Estates, Number Eleven.","Alpha Sebastian had discharged himself from Mercy General and come home against medical advice. Ethan tried soup, toast, even food from Alpha Sebastian’s favorite steakhouse. He refused all of it.","By evening, Ethan had run out of patience and called Alpha Roger and Luna Margaret.","They found Alpha Sebastian pale and running on fumes, taking calls from Hale Group between waves of stomach pain. He could barely stay on his feet, yet he still refused to let his Beta handle the Pack reports. With the board watching and patrol issues piling up along Hale territory, he could not afford to look absent.","When Luna Margaret learned Eira was staying at Number Nine, she drove over to get her.","She returned twenty minutes later with mud on her boots and a tear in the hem of her camel coat.","Alpha Roger looked her over. \"I take it she said no.\"","\"I never even saw her. That housekeeper threatened to call estate security, and those dogs wouldn’t stop barking.\"","Alpha Roger glanced at the torn wool. \"So you made a scene.\"","\"I asked Eira to come talk some sense into Alpha Sebastian.\" Luna Margaret stripped off the damaged coat and tossed it over a chair. \"She probably wasn’t even home. It’s after ten. God knows who she’s out with.\"","The insult came out by habit. For four years, finding fault with Eira had been second nature.","Then Luna Margaret remembered that Eira was no longer a Hale. She was free to date, join another Pack, or come home carrying another male’s scent. None of it was Luna Margaret’s business anymore.","That only made her angrier.","\"She’s divorced,\" she muttered. \"Let’s see how long Sterling keeps playing the hero.\"","\"Mother.\"","Alpha Sebastian stood in the doorway, his phone still in his hand. His face was bloodless, but his eyes had turned cold.","\"Why do you keep talking about her like that?\"","Luna Margaret’s expression changed at once. \"I didn’t mean anything by it. I made chicken noodle soup. Why don’t you try a few bites?\"","\"I’m not hungry.\"","\"You haven’t eaten all day.\"","\"I said no.\"","Luna Margaret finally lost her patience. \"What exactly are you trying to prove? Eira isn’t here to see this. You’re only scaring the people who still care about you.\"","Alpha Sebastian tightened his grip on the phone.","Luna Margaret saw the guilt on his face and pushed too far.","\"She walked away, Sebastian. She doesn’t care what happens to you. When are you going to get that through your head?\"","His eyes reddened.","Luna Margaret fell silent.","Alpha Roger watched his son from across the room. Alpha Sebastian looked terrible, but at least he was still answering company calls and reviewing Pack reports. He had not abandoned his responsibilities as Alpha.","Still, Alpha Roger had decided that the family would stay at Number Eleven until Alpha Sebastian recovered.","As for Eira, Alpha Roger did not believe four years could disappear with a signature.","If asking her directly had failed, Alpha Roger would find another way to reach her."]},{"number":203,"title":"Chapter 203 The Levee and the Ant","paragraphs":["The German shepherds started barking before sunrise.","Eira pulled on a robe and crossed to the front window. Alpha Roger Hale stood outside the gate, arguing with the security officer on duty.","\"I’m asking for five minutes,\" Alpha Roger said. \"Tell Eira I’m here.\"","\"I already told you, sir. Ms. Crawford isn’t receiving visitors.\" The officer gestured toward Alpha Roger’s car. \"You need to leave.\"","The noise brought Mrs. Jones onto the porch, phone in hand.","\"You’ve got to be kidding me,\" she called. \"Your wife was here last night. Are the Hales taking shifts now?\"","Alpha Roger turned, already annoyed. \"This is a private family matter.\"","\"Eira divorced your son. You’re not her family anymore.\"","\"I didn’t come here to argue with the help.\"","Mrs. Jones gave him a tight smile. \"Keep talking like that, and ’the help’ will have the police remove you.\"","Before Alpha Roger could answer, Eira stepped outside.","\"It’s okay, Mrs. Jones. I’ve got this.\"","Alpha Roger faced her. \"Finally.\"","Eira stayed on the porch. \"Say what you came to say. Then leave.\"","\"You’re going to make me stand at the gate?\"","\"You showed up at my home before sunrise without an invitation. You’re lucky I came outside at all.\"","Alpha Roger glanced at the security officers. He had spent years as Hale Pack’s Alpha, and he clearly hated being kept outside like an unwanted salesman.","\"Think this through, Eira,\" he said, lowering his voice. \"You’re the public face of a federal tech project now. A scene with the Hale family could hurt your work with Sterling.\"","\"Then don’t make a scene.\" She folded her arms. \"Or call the press yourself. Tell them you came here to pressure your son’s ex-wife into taking care of him. I’m sure the Pack Council will love that story.\"","His expression tightened. With rumors already circling Alpha Sebastian and the Hale Pack, Alpha Roger knew the threat would hurt them more than it would hurt her.","When he spoke again, some of the edge was gone.","\"Sebastian is sick. He left the hospital too soon, he won’t eat, and he won’t listen to anyone. Just come talk to him.\"","\"No.\"","\"Eira, you were married for four years.\"","\"And now we’re divorced.\"","\"He’s falling apart because you left.\"","Eira stared at him. \"Sebastian checked himself out against medical advice. He’s refusing food and working himself sick. Those are his choices, not mine.\"","\"You know why he’s doing it.\"","\"Then he needs a therapist along with a doctor. He doesn’t need his ex-wife.\"","Alpha Roger wrapped one hand around the iron gate. \"How can you shut him out after everything you shared?\"","The question might have hurt once. Now it only made Eira tired.","\"We didn’t share much of anything,\" Eira said. \"I cooked his meals, ran his home, and carried the duties of a Luna while your family treated me like I should be grateful for a place at the table.\"","Alpha Roger’s jaw tightened, but she did not let him interrupt.","\"The affair was the last straw. It wasn’t the whole reason I left. For four years, Sebastian stood by while your family wore me down. He saw it, and he did nothing.\"","Silence settled between them.","Alpha Roger had come expecting the devoted wife who used to drop everything whenever Alpha Sebastian needed her. That woman was gone, and for the first time, he seemed to see it.","\"I gave your son four years,\" Eira said. \"He doesn’t get the rest of my life too.\"","Alpha Roger looked away. \"So that’s it?\"","\"That’s it. Take him back to Mercy General. Make him follow the doctor’s orders. But stop sending people here to make his health my responsibility.\"","She looked toward the security officer.","\"Please make sure Mr. Hale leaves. If he comes back without an invitation, call the police.\"","\"Yes, ma’am.\"","Eira went inside. A moment later, Alpha Roger’s car pulled away and the gate slid shut behind it.","Mrs. Jones locked the front door. \"Your new place can’t be ready soon enough.\"","\"I called the contractor yesterday. We’re only waiting on the security inspection at Ten Ashford Lane.\"","\"Good. Because I’m done waking up to Hales on the lawn.\"","Eira glanced through the window at the empty driveway.","Moving would give her more privacy, but it would not fix the real problem. The Hales had barely noticed her while she belonged to them.","Now that she was gone, they refused to let her go.","After breakfast, a black Sterling SUV pulled up outside Number Nine. Eira expected to find Alpha Killian in the back, but the driver stepped out alone and opened the door for her.","\"Alpha Killian had to leave the country early this morning,\" he said. \"An acquisition ran into trouble. His flight took off around five, and he didn’t want to wake you.\"","\"He sent you to pick me up?\"","\"He asked me to stay available while he’s away. If you need a ride, just text me.\"","\"I’m perfectly capable of calling an Uber.\"","\"I know, ma’am.\" The driver smiled. \"Think of me as Plan B.\"","That sounded exactly like Alpha Killian. Protective without admitting he was being protective.","Eira climbed in. A steady winter rain had slowed the morning traffic to a crawl. Commuters hurried along the sidewalks under umbrellas, clutching coffee as the SUV moved through the gray Palo Alto streets.","At the R&D center, she found Miles near the elevators with a latte in one hand and his phone in the other.","\"Aren’t you supposed to be off?\"","\"That was the plan.\" He pocketed his phone. \"The overseas acquisition hit an antitrust snag. The seller threatened to walk unless Alpha Killian showed up in person, so he flew out with Kate. Natalie’s covering the home front, and I came in to help.\"","\"When will he be back?\"","\"No clue. The lawyers are still trying to untangle the regulatory mess.\"","Eira knew Alpha Killian carried a lot. Sterling Group, Council votes, Pack resources, and security along the territorial borders all demanded his attention. Even so, before boarding an international flight, he had arranged a driver for her.","Miles watched her for a moment. \"If anything comes up while he’s gone, call me.\"","\"I thought you were taking comp time.\"","\"I’m bad at taking time off.\"","\"I can take care of myself.\"","\"I know.\" His expression softened. \"Call anyway. Work, Pack trouble, personal drama. Whatever it is, I’ve got you.\"","It was almost exactly what the driver had said.","Eira narrowed her eyes. \"Miles, you work for Killian.\"","\"Last time I checked.\"","\"Then why is everyone acting like they works for me?\"","Miles took a slow sip of his latte. A knowing smile spread across his face.","\"Have a good morning, Ms. Crawford.\"","Before she could press him, he stepped into the waiting elevator and let the doors slide shut."]},{"number":204,"title":"Chapter 204 Present in His Absence","paragraphs":["Before entering the secure underground lab, everyone had to leave phones and smartwatches in a locked cabinet. Eira was about to put hers away when Alpha Killian’s name flashed across the screen.","Killian: Had to fly overseas. No return date yet. The driver will stay available. Call Miles if you need anything.","Brief and direct. Still, he had taken the time to tell her himself.","Eira stepped aside as another engineer moved through security.","Eira: Okay. Heading into the lab now.","Killian: Good. Don’t skip lunch.","The reply came so fast that she smiled.","Eira: No promises.","She locked up her phone, changed into a clean-room suit, and passed through the airlock.","By the time she finished, it was after five. She showered, changed back into her clothes, and collected her phone before heading upstairs.","Lila was waiting outside the secure elevators in jeans and an oversized Stanford hoodie, holding two iced coffees.","\"There she is,\" Lila said. \"The woman who stood up an entire lunch.\"","Eira glanced at the drinks. \"You’re giving me coffee after five?\"","\"One’s decaf. I’m not completely irresponsible.\"","\"What are you doing here?\"","\"Running a rescue mission.\" Lila linked arms with her and steered her toward Sterling Tower. \"Natalie had lunch delivered to the lab staging area. Four hours later, it was still sitting there untouched, so she called me.\"","Eira sighed. \"You people have a whole surveillance network.\"","\"We call it caring. Try not to fight it.\"","Mrs. Jones was waiting in the executive lounge with a canvas food carrier open on the table. She had packed roast chicken, wild rice, green beans, and warm apple crisp.","The moment Eira walked in, Mrs. Jones pointed to a chair.","\"Sit. Eat.\"","\"I lost track of time.\"","\"You always lose track of time.\" Mrs. Jones filled a plate and set it in front of her. \"That excuse is getting old.\"","Eira sat down. \"I’m sorry.\"","\"Eat first. Apologize later.\"","Lila dropped into the chair across from her. \"She practiced that speech in the car.\"","\"I did not,\" Mrs. Jones said.","\"You absolutely did.\"","Eira took a bite of chicken. Both women watched her.","\"Are you going to stare at me until I finish?\"","\"Yes,\" they said together.","Her phone rang before she could argue. Susan’s name appeared on the screen.","\"Hi, Susan.\"","\"The demand letters went out this afternoon,\" Susan said. \"Certified mail, overnight courier, and copies to authorized counsel. Everything is documented.\"","\"When does the deadline start?\"","\"Tomorrow. They have ten calendar days to respond. I’ll call you the second either side makes a move.\"","\"Thank you.\"","Eira ended the call and looked across the table.","\"The letters are out.\"","Lila’s face lit up. She raised her plastic cup.","\"To being officially done with their crap.\"","Mrs. Jones lifted her water glass. \"I’ll drink to that.\"","Eira smiled and raised her own.","\"So will I.\"","--","The demand letter reached the Winthrop estate that afternoon. A housekeeper signed for the courier envelope, then called Serena.","\"Ms. Winthrop, a legal envelope came for you. You just missed it.\"","Serena had left less than thirty minutes earlier, but she had no interest in turning around.","\"Put it on the desk in my grandfather’s study. I’ll get it later.\"","She ended the call. It was probably paperwork from Ryan Sullivan’s company.","Serena had spent the afternoon convincing Alpha Victor to support Ryan’s medical chip venture.","At first, her grandfather had dismissed it as commercial R&D. No federal funding, no academic publications, and no prestige for the Winthrop name. The patents would belong to Ryan’s company.","But the technology could fill a major gap in the medical market. If it worked, Serena could use the project to rebuild her career.","Alpha Victor had finally agreed to make a few introductions. Then he had asked how things stood with Vincent.","Serena had avoided the question. She had not told him about the pregnancy. She had only said Alpha Sebastian’s divorce was final.","Even that had made the old Alpha’s expression turn cold. He guarded the Winthrop name as fiercely as he guarded Pack territory, and he would never approve of his granddaughter having a baby with a man whose divorce was still fresh enough to dominate the Pack rumor mill.","Serena had left before he could press her.","She had somewhere else to be.","Ethan had told her Alpha Sebastian had barely eaten since leaving Mercy General. If he let himself fall apart, who would protect her and the baby?","She had no intention of ending the pregnancy. As long as she carried Alpha Sebastian’s child, he could not cut her out of his life completely.","She drove straight to Southridge Estates.","At Number Eleven, security stopped her at the gate. Isabella was outside unloading boxes when she spotted Serena’s car.","Her face darkened, but she quickly hid it.","\"Let her in,\" Isabella told the guard. \"She’s my guest.\"","Serena still had to show her ID and sign the visitor log. By the time she parked, Isabella was waiting with her phone in hand.","\"So it’s true?\" Isabella asked. \"You’re pregnant?\"","Serena glanced at the phone. The camera was pointed straight at her.","\"Are you recording me?\"","\"Absolutely. I’m done taking your word for anything.\" Isabella raised the phone higher. \"Is my brother the father?\"","Serena knew better than to answer. Isabella had never been good at hiding a scheme, and this one was painfully obvious.","\"Where is Sebastian?\"","Isabella laughed. \"Nice dodge.\"","She stopped recording and stepped aside. \"He’s upstairs. Don’t expect a warm welcome.\"","Inside, Alpha Roger and Luna Margaret went still when they saw Serena.","Luna Margaret folded her arms. \"What are you doing here?\"","\"I came to see Sebastian.\" Serena rested a hand lightly over her stomach. \"We also need to talk about the baby.\"","Luna Margaret’s gaze dropped to the gesture. Her face tightened.","\"He’s upstairs.\"","Serena headed for the staircase.","Isabella followed. \"Don’t think a baby makes you family.\"","\"Enough,\" Luna Margaret warned.","\"What? Sebastian never asked for a kid with her. She thinks getting pregnant is some kind of golden ticket.\"","Serena tightened her grip on her leather tote but kept walking. Picking a fight in the Hale home would get her nowhere.","At the top of the stairs, she stopped outside Alpha Sebastian’s bedroom, lifted her chin, and opened the door.","He was on the phone.","\"No,\" Alpha Sebastian said, his voice cold. \"I want the full Snowmark report tonight. If the numbers don’t match, find out who changed them.\"","Serena stayed in the doorway and waited for him to notice her."]},{"number":205,"title":"Chapter 205 The Pup Card","paragraphs":["At the sound of the door, Alpha Sebastian expected his mother or Isabella.","Serena walked in instead.","His jaw tightened. \"I’ll call you back.\" He ended the call and set his phone on the desk. \"What are you doing here?\"","\"I heard you were home from the hospital.\" Serena gave him a small, worried smile. \"I wanted to check on you.\"","He looked worse than she had expected. His face was pale, his cheeks hollow, and an untouched breakfast tray sat beside his laptop.","Serena had known him since they were teenagers. He had been part of her life for ten years, and some part of her still cared about him.","But the way he looked at her now, cold and distant, hurt more than she wanted to admit.","\"You need to eat something,\" she said. \"If you won’t do it for yourself, at least think about the baby.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s eyes dropped to her stomach. \"We’ve already had this conversation. \"I don’t want a life with you.\"","\"It’s not that simple.\" She rested a hand over her abdomen. \"My doctor said ending the pregnancy could cause complications. I might not be able to get pregnant again.\"","The lie came easily.","Alpha Sebastian had once wanted a pup to keep Eira tied to him. Now Serena intended to use this baby to keep him from walking away.","\"You know I’ve always had health issues,\" she continued. \"I’m twenty-eight, Seb. This could be my only chance to have a pup. Are you really asking me to give that up?\"","A flicker of hesitation crossed his face.","Serena moved closer. \"Whatever happened between us, this baby is still yours.\"","Alpha Sebastian looked away. \"Have you thought about what happens if you keep it?\"","\"We raise our pup.\"","\"No.\" His answer was immediate. \"There is no ...we.’ I won’t bond with you, and I can’t give you the future you want.\"","Her face tightened. \"So you’ll just turn your back on your own pup?\"","\"I’ll take responsibility for the pup. Financially and legally.\" He met her eyes. \"But that doesn’t make us a couple, and it doesn’t make this pup the Hale heir.\"","\"Because you’re still holding out for Eira?\"","\"Yes.\"","Serena stared at him, almost laughing at the absurdity of it.","Eira had divorced him and severed their mate bond. Alpha Sebastian had spent years using their marital assets to support another woman. No amount of regret could erase that.","Eira had loved him once. Everyone had seen it. But the deeper the love, the worse the betrayal. Serena could not believe Eira would ever take him back.","\"Seb, listen to yourself.\" She let tears gather in her eyes. \"Eira left. She’s moving on with her life. I’m the one who came back. I’m here, and I’m carrying your baby. We still have a chance to build something together.\"","Alpha Sebastian was silent for a long moment.","Then he let out a bitter laugh.","\"You’re right.\"","Hope flashed across Serena’s face.","\"I should have seen the woman who was right in front of me.\"","She took a step toward him. \"Exactly.\"","\"For four years,\" he said quietly, \"that woman was Eira.\"","Serena’s smile disappeared.","\"She was there every day, and I treated her like she didn’t matter. I won’t make that mistake again.\"","\"She left you,\" Serena said, her voice tightening. \"Whatever you had is over.\"","\"What’s over is you and me.\" Alpha Sebastian met her gaze. \"The day I bonded with Eira, you should have become part of my past. I was too selfish to let go. That was my mistake.\"","Serena’s control began to crack.","\"Do you really want her?\" she asked. \"Or do you want the award-winning scientist everyone suddenly cares about?\"","Alpha Sebastian’s eyes turned cold.","\"Before Eira’s name was all over the news, you didn’t even believe she could be Dr. Crawford,\" Serena continued. \"When I told you the scientist from our lab had the same name as your wife, you laughed. You said Eira should be flattered by the comparison.\"","She gave him a bitter smile.","\"So don’t stand there and pretend you loved her all along.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s face tightened. Serena knew at once that she had pushed too far. Instead of turning him against Eira, she had only reminded him of how badly he had treated her.","She quickly changed course.","\"I know I lied about the Sovereign Processor Initiative,\" she said, letting her voice soften. \"I wasn’t the project lead. But you spent ten years believing in me, and I was terrified you’d see me as a failure. By the time I realized how far the lie had gone, I didn’t know how to take it back.\"","Then she lifted her chin. \"But I’m not washed up. Ryan Sullivan is launching a medical chip project, and he asked my grandfather to bring me on as lead researcher. I still have a career, Seb. I still have something to offer.\"","\"That was never the point,\" Alpha Sebastian said.","\"Then what is?\"","His answer came without hesitation.","\"I can’t lose Eira.\"","Serena went still.","Anything she said now would only push him closer to Eira. She had returned believing she could take back her place in his life. Instead, Eira had filed for divorce, walked away, and become the one woman Alpha Sebastian could not let go.","So Serena played the only card she had left.","\"Then forget about us for a minute.\" She pulled an ultrasound printout from her leather tote. \"Just look at your baby.\"","Alpha Sebastian did not reach for it.","\"There’s a heartbeat now,\" she continued. \"The doctor said everything looks normal.\"","His gaze dropped to the image. There was little more than a dark oval and a tiny blur, but the report at the bottom was clear.","Cardiac activity detected.","For the first time, his expression shifted.","Serena moved closer. \"That’s your pup, Seb. Your firstborn.\"","She took his hand and placed it against her stomach.","Alpha Sebastian stiffened, but he did not pull away at once.","It was far too early to feel movement. He knew that. Still, the ultrasound had made the pregnancy real in a way Serena’s words had not.","His pup was growing inside her."]},{"number":206,"title":"Chapter 206 The Snow Day","paragraphs":["Alpha Sebastian finally told Serena to go home.","He had not agreed to accept the baby as his heir, but he had studied the ultrasound and allowed her to place his hand on her stomach. For now, that was enough. She had found a weak spot.","On her way out, Serena paused in the living room with one hand resting on her belly. She did not say a word. She did not need to.","The front door had barely closed when Isabella turned to Luna Margaret.","\"Was that little performance really necessary?\"","Luna Margaret kept staring at the door. \"Your brother may be changing his mind about the baby.\"","\"Great. So she gets exactly what she wants?\" Isabella folded her arms. \"And what happens if Alpha Sebastian is still trying to win Eira back?\"","Alpha Roger let out a tired sigh. \"Eira isn’t coming back to him.\"","Isabella frowned. \"How do you know? She used to worship the ground he walked on.\"","Alpha Roger did not answer.","That morning, Eira had made it painfully clear that there was nothing left to save.","The study door opened before Isabella could ask anything else.","Alpha Sebastian walked into the kitchen with his phone in hand. Everyone fell quiet.","He had refused food all day. Now he took a container of chicken noodle soup from the refrigerator and put it in the microwave.","Luna Margaret started to get up, but Alpha Roger stopped her with a look.","Alpha Sebastian set his phone on the counter. His last exchange with Jordan was still open.","Jordan: The storm grounded most flights out of D.C. tonight. I’ll have to rebook.","A second message followed.","Jordan: They’re calling for the first snow of the season near Klamath Mountains tomorrow. Doesn’t that mean Ms. Crawford’s birthday is coming up?","Alpha Sebastian stared at the screen.","Palo Alto would only get cold rain. The snow was hundreds of miles north, in the mountains where Eira had grown up.","But that was the snow that mattered.","No one knew Eira’s real birthday.","Miss Gwen had found her outside an Omega group home in the mountains of Northern California during the first snowfall of the year.","With no records and no family coming forward to claim her, Miss Gwen had used that date on Eira’s intake forms.","That date became her official birthday and never changed.","Privately, though, Eira celebrated whenever the first snow returned to those mountains.","Alpha Sebastian had once asked her why.","She had gone quiet, and Miss Gwen had answered for her.","\"She’s still hoping someone remembers,\" Miss Gwen had told him. \"Maybe her family lost her in that first snow. If they hear her story someday, they might recognize it. She likes to believe she wasn’t abandoned. Maybe she was only lost.\"","Eira had never admitted that herself.","Years later, while they watched a livestream of snow falling over Klamath Mountains, she had asked him, \"Don’t you think it’s kind of romantic? Waiting for winter to decide when your birthday starts?\"","Alpha Sebastian had smiled. \"You? Romantic?\"","\"You never know exactly when the first snow will come. Maybe November. Maybe December.\" She had watched the flakes cover the mountain road. \"Then one morning, everything up there turns white, and suddenly it’s my birthday.\"","\"I thought you liked things you could count on.\"","\"I do.\" She had looked at him and smiled. \"That’s what I have you for.\"","The microwave beeped, pulling him back to the kitchen.","Alpha Sebastian closed his eyes.","She had once believed he was the safest, surest thing in her life. He had taken that trust and broken it.","He carried the soup to the island and sat down. His family might think Serena had convinced him to eat. He did not bother correcting them.","The first snow was coming to Klamath Mountains.","So was Eira’s birthday.","--","Serena had barely left Number Eleven when her phone buzzed.","Lainey: Free for drinks tonight?","That evening, Lainey sat in a corner booth at a quiet hotel bar, reviewing the notes on her tablet.","For days, she had tried to make sense of the mess around Eira. Vincent gave her vague answers. Logan had only just returned from overseas. Fiona clearly knew more than she was willing to share, and Finn was useless. The second Eira’s name came up, he turned into her biggest fan.","Still, Lainey had worked out the basics.","Eira had loved Alpha Sebastian. Alpha Sebastian had chosen Serena. Now Alpha Sebastian wanted Eira back, Serena wanted to hold on to Alpha Sebastian, and Alpha Killian seemed determined to claim a place in Eira’s life.","Then there was Lainey, who had wanted Alpha Killian for years.","But none of that explained why Eira looked so familiar, or why learning she was an orphan had hit Lainey so hard.","When Serena entered the bar, Lainey locked her tablet and slipped it into her bag.","\"Serena. Glad you could make it.\"","Serena slid into the booth and set her leather tote beside her. \"You disappeared on me. What have you been up to?\"","\"A campaign shoot for the Carters. It took over my life for a few days.\" Lainey waved to the server, then poured Serena a glass of water from the bottle on the table. \"Plus, my family still acts like I’ll drop dead if I stay out past nine.\"","Serena knew about Lainey’s heart condition. \"I thought you were here on vacation. I didn’t realize you were working.\"","\"I like staying busy.\" Lainey gave her a measured smile. \"You apparently do too. Pregnant, and you’re already lining up another research project.\"","Serena’s shoulders stiffened. \"Vincent told you?\"","\"He mentioned it.\"","\"He promised to keep the pregnancy private.\"","Lainey caught the concern in her voice.\"So where do things stand with your boyfriend?Should I expect wedding invitations anytime soon?\"","\"We’re taking things one day at a time,\" Serena said lightly, though a flicker of unease flashed in her eyes.","Then she steered the conversation away from herself.","\"What about Eira? You brought her up the last time we talked, but you never told me why.\"","Lainey looked down at her drink, pretending to hesitate.","\"Promise you won’t laugh?\"","\"Of course.\"","\"I’ve had a thing for Killian Sterling for years.\" She let out a self-conscious laugh. \"A serious thing. Unfortunately, he only seems to have eyes for Eira. He even took her home to meet his parents.\"","Serena leaned back. \"I didn’t know it had gone that far.\"","\"Neither did I.\" Lainey traced one finger around the rim of her glass. \"She came out of nowhere. No family, no Pack, no bloodline anyone can trace. Now she’s working with Sterling Group and having dinner with Killian’s parents like she already belongs there.\"","She let just enough resentment enter her voice.","Serena’s mood lifted at once.","Lainey was jealous of Eira.","For the first time all day, Serena felt like she had caught a break."]},{"number":207,"title":"Chapter 207 The Shelter in the Mountains","paragraphs":["\"I know Eira,\" Serena said, bitterness sharpening her voice. \"She’s not the saint everyone makes her out to be. Sebastian is still obsessed with her. He’s so desperate to get her back that he doesn’t even want his own baby.\"","Lainey paused with her wine halfway to her lips.\"If Alpha Sebastian is chasing his ex-wife while you’re carrying his child, that’s messy,\"","\"And now Alpha Killian’s involved. One ugly headline could turn into a political headache for both Packs.\"","\"Exactly.\" Serena leaned closer. \"Finally, someone gets it.\"","Lainey took a slow sip of wine, studying her over the rim. Serena mistook good manners for sympathy. That was fine. Growing up Crawford had taught Lainey how to smile through almost any conversation.","\"How well do you actually know Eira?\" she asked. \"The articles say she grew up in an Omega group home, but they never name it. Do you know where it was?\"","Public searches had turned up nothing. Eira’s childhood records were sealed, and the few official profiles about her jumped straight from the group home to Stanford.","Serena gave a dismissive shrug. \"What is there to know? She grew up with nothing, got a scholarship, and lucked into Dr. Thorne’s lab. Then he handed her his entire project.\"","\"She got lucky,\" Lainey said, letting the insult pass. \"But I still want the name of the group home.\"","\"I don’t know it. Sebastian might.\" Serena thought for a moment. \"He used to take Eira back every year. Check the Carter Foundation’s donation records. I remember hearing that the place was somewhere in the mountains near the Oregon border.\"","The Oregon border.","Lainey’s fingers tightened around the stem of her glass.","Crawford Pack’s northwestern territory ran through the Klamath Mountains and western Siskiyou County. Henry had spent years stationed there.","\"Why do you care which group home it was?\" Serena asked.","Lainey relaxed her grip. \"I want to know what Alpha Killian sees in her.\"","She gave a small, embarrassed laugh and added just enough jealousy to make it believable.","\"If I’m going up against her, I should at least know who I’m dealing with.\"","Serena nodded, satisfied. \"Smart. But Alpha Killian took her home to meet his parents? The Sterlings can’t be happy about that.\"","\"They’re being polite.\" Lainey swirled her wine. \"Alpha Killian may be Alpha, but an old Pack like Sterling comes with a lot of voices. His mother’s family, the Reeds, has opinions about everything, especially who carries on the bloodline.\"","The Sterling and Reed Packs had been joined through a strategic mate bond. Behind Alpha Killian stood generations of relatives who treated marriage like Pack policy. Luna Seraphina had spent years keeping the Reed elders from pushing their handpicked heiresses at him.","An orphaned, wolfless Omega with no Pack or known bloodline should never have made it past the front door.","Unless Eira was not who everyone thought she was.","Unless the resemblance to Henry was more than a coincidence.","The thought turned Lainey’s stomach.","She set down her glass before Serena noticed her hand shaking.","--","Two days later, Lainey sat across from Fiona Carter in a glass-walled office overlooking downtown.","At their last campaign meeting, Lainey had suggested pairing the new brand shoot with a charity feature. The same model could appear in two separate campaigns, one commercial and one focused on community work.","Fiona, recently promoted to brand director, had liked the idea but wanted time to review it.","Now Lainey placed a gallery invitation on her desk.","\"There’s a photographer I met during a shoot in Milan,\" she said. \"He’s showing new work downtown next month. I’m not really interested in the gallery crowd, so I thought you might enjoy it.\"","Fiona picked up the invitation. She could get into almost any gallery, but reaching the artists themselves was another story.","\"Thanks.\" She looked at Lainey. \"What do you want?\"","Lainey smiled. \"Nothing dramatic. I thought you might let me see the Carter Foundation’s charity records. I’m helping put together the community campaign, and I want to understand where the brand has invested in the past.\"","Fiona studied her for a moment, then unlocked her phone.","\"Fine. My father wants me to handle the year-end donations anyway. I’ve been going through the files.\"","She opened the foundation’s records and waved Lainey over.","Lainey stood beside her, careful not to touch the phone. Fiona scrolled through pages of donations to schools, food banks, medical clinics, and Omega support programs.","Then Lainey saw it.","The same small group home appeared four years in a row.","\"Hold on.\"","Fiona stopped scrolling. \"What?\"","Lainey pointed to the screen. \"That location looks beautiful. All those mountains and fog. Is it near the Oregon border?\"","Fiona gave her a skeptical look. \"Are you choosing charities based on the view now?\"","\"I’ve never been there.\" Lainey kept her tone light. \"I like finding new places.\"","Fiona shrugged and closed the file. \"Good luck with that.\"","Lainey thanked her and left.","Fiona returned to work, but the file stayed in the back of her mind. A recurring donation was not unusual. The amounts were modest, the paperwork was clean, and every payment had passed the foundation’s review.","Still, four consecutive years felt personal.","She opened the record again and checked the delivery logs.","One name appeared on every trip.","Sebastian Hale.","Fiona leaned back in her chair.","Why had Alpha Sebastian personally delivered supplies to the same remote group home every year?"]},{"number":208,"title":"Chapter 208 A Recurring Name","paragraphs":["What could Lainey possibly want with Sebastian?","Fiona went over the facts again. Lainey’s brother, Vincent, was still wrapped around Serena’s finger, and Serena was carrying Sebastian’s baby. None of that explained why Lainey was digging into a group home in the Klamath Mountains.","Fiona wrote down the shelter’s name and location, then called the Carter Foundation’s community relations office.","\"I’m reviewing the donation history for one of our approved charities,\" she said. \"Can you tell me how that group home was added to the list?\"","\"It started with a private donation from Mr. Hale,\" the coordinator explained. \"After that, he referred the shelter to us. Our compliance and public relations teams completed the review, and we added it to the approved list.\"","\"Does Sebastian still donate to it every year?\"","\"Not directly. The foundation handles the payments, and the shelter has been selected several times through our annual program. I don’t have the full delivery history in front of me.\"","\"Could you send me the records?\"","\"I can send the public files. If you need details about Mr. Hale’s personal involvement, you’ll have to ask him.\"","Fiona frowned. \"And everything is clean?\"","\"Completely. The donations were reviewed and documented.\"","\"Good. Thanks for your help.\"","She hung up, drummed her nails against the desk, and called Finn.","\"Finn, did you know Sebastian personally delivered supplies to a group home in the Klamath Mountains every year?\"","\"A group home?\" Finn paused. \"I don’t know much about it, but Eira once mentioned growing up in one.\"","His voice sharpened immediately. Anything connected to Eira got his full attention.","\"Why? What did you find?\"","Fiona looked at the donation records on her screen.","Suddenly, the pieces fit.","Lainey was not trying to learn more about Vincent or Serena. She was investigating Eira. And she had a reason.","The Crawford family was close to Luna Seraphina. For years, the Reed elders had treated Lainey as a possible match for Alpha Killian. Now Alpha Killian had publicly chosen Eira at the Wood family clinic.","Fiona lowered her voice.","\"Finn, you need to warn Eira. Lainey found the group home where she grew up.\"","Finn went quiet.","Fiona felt a pang of sympathy for Eira. She had already been betrayed by Alpha Sebastian. Now the Hale family was pressuring him to keep the divorce quiet and stop Eira from speaking publicly. They were treating her reputation and silence like problems they could manage.","Maybe Alpha Sebastian had negotiated a private settlement with her. Maybe he had not.","Either way, the Carters were prepared.","If Alpha Sebastian kept the scandal under control and protected the Snowmark project, the board would let him remain CEO. If he failed, they would vote him out without hesitation.","--","Alpha Sebastian’s burner phone buzzed.","The message was from Finn, but it was clearly meant for Eira.","[Eira, Lainey found the group home where you grew up.]","Alpha Sebastian stared at the screen, then typed a reply in the casual tone Eira usually used.","[Who’s Lainey?]","Finn took a moment to answer.","[You don’t remember her? She was with Vincent at dinner. His sister.]","Another message came through.","[The Reed elders have been pushing her as a possible match for Killian. She’s into him.]","Then Finn added:","[Watch your back, Eira. She looks sweet, but she was raised a Crawford.]","Alpha Sebastian read the warning twice before replying.","[Got it.]","He lowered the phone, but his thoughts were already racing.","If Lainey wanted Alpha Killian, why was she digging into Eira’s past?","Unless Alpha Killian and Eira were more serious than he had believed.","At the Wood family clinic, Alpha Killian had called Eira his girlfriend, and Eira had confirmed it. Alpha Sebastian had assumed they were only putting on a show to provoke him.","But Lainey’s investigation changed everything.","She would not be searching for Eira’s childhood records unless Alpha Killian had taken Eira seriously. He might have already introduced her to the Sterling family and the Reed elders, the people who guarded their bloodline and Pack alliances like national security.","Eira had met Alpha Killian’s family.","She had done it almost immediately after leaving Alpha Sebastian.","Jealousy flashed through him, followed by a sharp wave of panic. The stomach ulcer that had finally eased over the past few days began to burn again.","He did not forward Finn’s warning to Eira.","A selfish part of him wanted Lainey to ruin things between Eira and Alpha Killian. If she succeeded, Eira might still come back to him.","Before he could put the phone away, Jordan called.","\"Alpha Sebastian, Snowmark wants to meet for dinner tomorrow night. There’s one condition.\"","Alpha Sebastian straightened. \"What condition?\"","\"They want you to bring your Luna.\"","Jordan chose the word carefully.","Alpha Sebastian’s hand tightened around the phone.","Snowmark had built its entire negotiation strategy around Eira’s reputation and technical work.","If Snowmark learned that Alpha Sebastian had divorced Eira after benefiting from her name, they could pull out.","The board would blame him.","His position at Hale Group would be in jeopardy, and his standing as an Alpha would take a serious hit.","Jordan waited for his answer.","\"I’ll be there,\" Alpha Sebastian said.","\"With Eira Crawford?\"","Alpha Sebastian closed his eyes. \"I’ll handle it.\"","\"Yes, Alpha.\"","Jordan ended the call. A moment later, the front desk called his office.","\"Jordan, three packages have been waiting for nearly a week. One is marked urgent and requires a signature. Should I send them up?\"","\"Send all three.\"","A few minutes later, two boxes and a courier envelope arrived on Jordan’s desk.","He opened the urgent envelope first. Inside was another plain white envelope, sealed and unmarked.","That was unusual. The outer packet had already been logged and photographed, but the inner envelope had no sender listed. It could contain confidential legal documents, so Jordan left it unopened.","When Alpha Sebastian arrived, Jordan handed it to him.","\"This was inside the courier packet. There’s no description on the label. It may be a personal letter.\"","Alpha Sebastian turned the envelope over. \"Who sends letters anymore?\"","He tore it open.","The first line made his stomach drop.","LEGAL NOTICE","To: Sebastian Hale, Hale Group, Inc.","Bishop & Marsh Attorneys, acting on behalf of our client, Eira Crawford, hereby give formal notice regarding marital assets transferred during the parties’ mate bond, without our client’s knowledge or consent, to a third party named Serena Winthrop..."]},{"number":209,"title":"Chapter 209 A Cruel Little Move","paragraphs":["The legal notice came in two parts, and both hit Alpha Sebastian hard.","The first explained the claim in clear, formal language. Under Pack Council law, the assets Alpha Sebastian had acquired during his registered mate bond with Eira were considered marital property.","That included the luxury cars, real estate, jewelry, and other high-value assets he had transferred to Serena without Eira’s knowledge or consent.","According to the notice, those transfers were invalid. Alpha Sebastian and Serena were both responsible for returning approximately $118 million to Eira.","The second page contained Susan’s firm’s formal demand.","Alpha Sebastian and Serena were given ten days to respond and begin returning any funds or assets determined to belong to Eira.","If they failed to comply, the firm would file suit on Eira’s behalf and seek the disputed assets, court costs, and any recoverable legal fees.","Alpha Sebastian’s fingers tightened around the pages. His eyes burned as he read the total again.","Eira was really doing this.","She was taking him to court over the money.","Jordan read the notice over his shoulder. His stomach dropped when he saw the amount.","There was a reason old Pack families warned people not to mistake a quiet wolf for a harmless one. The quiet ones rarely lost control. When they finally did, everyone nearby paid the price.","\"Alpha,\" Jordan said carefully, \"the Snowmark project is about to launch. If Eira files in federal court, this could cause serious damage.\"","Alpha Sebastian already knew.","The lawsuit would reach the press, the Hale Group board, the Pack Council, and every potential partner watching the company. If the scandal became public, the board would push him out and bury him in some meaningless executive position until he quit.","His stomach burned. A sharp pulse throbbed behind his eyes.","\"Eira,\" he muttered. \"Did it really have to come to this?\"","Then he looked at the deadline again, and his expression hardened.","\"Find Serena. She received the same notice. Tell her to sell whatever she can. If she can’t liquidate everything in time, she needs to find another way to cover the balance. Every dollar goes back to Eira.\"","Jordan glanced at the date stamped on the notice.","The color drained from his face.","\"Alpha, we only have four days left.\"","Alpha Sebastian looked up. \"What?\"","\"The courier delivered the packet six days ago.\" Jordan swallowed. \"Reception signed for it, but no one sent it upstairs.\"","Alpha Sebastian stared at him. \"Six days ago?\"","\"Yes, Alpha.\"","\"You’re telling me the ten-day deadline started six days ago?\"","\"That’s what the delivery record says.\"","Alpha Sebastian crushed the corner of the notice in his fist.","\"Why the hell wasn’t I told the day it arrived?\" he shouted. \"What is reception doing down there?\"","Jordan had no answer ready. He had been in Klamath following leads, and while he was gone, the legal notice had slipped through the cracks.","He recovered quickly.","\"Alpha, the outer packet didn’t list any contents. It looked like routine mail. Inside was a plain envelope, and the legal notice was sealed inside that.\"","Sebastian’s expression hardened.","\"Three layers,\" Jordan said. \"Whoever sent it knew exactly how to make sure it sat in reception without drawing attention.\"","Alpha Sebastian understood the message. Eira could have filed the lawsuit without warning. Instead, the notice had been delivered in a way that made the threat impossible to ignore.","But Eira was not vindictive. She was controlled, careful, and private. She would not turn a legal notice into a personal attack.","\"No,\" Alpha Sebastian said. \"Eira didn’t do this. Alpha Killian did.\"","Killian Sterling had always gotten under his skin. He had inherited money, power, an old bloodline, and control of both the Sterling Pack and its corporate empire. He had never needed to fight for his place.","Now he had taken Eira’s side and turned her anger against Alpha Sebastian.","Alpha Sebastian grabbed the water glass from his desk and threw it at the wall. It shattered, sending glass and water across the floor.","Jordan waited until the room fell silent.","\"Alpha, the lawsuit is not the most urgent problem. If Eira files against Serena, the divorce will become public. Snowmark’s executives still expect you to bring your Luna to dinner tomorrow night.\"","Alpha Sebastian dragged a hand over his face.","If the Snowmark team learned that Eira was no longer his mate, they could walk away from the deal. The project was too important, and he could not let the company take the fall for his personal mess.","That left him with one option.","He had to see Eira and convince her to attend the dinner as his Luna.","The thought made his chest tighten. After everything he had done, he had no right to ask her for one more favor.","But he had to try.","\"The Klamath lead has been handled,\" Jordan said carefully.","Alpha Sebastian’s chest tightened.","Sam was the only reason Eira might agree to see him. It was a desperate plan, but he had nothing else. Their mate bond was gone, and the divorce was final. He needed one chance to explain himself.","\"Did you set up a local number?\" Alpha Sebastian asked.","\"Yes. A prepaid phone with a 530 area code. It made things easier in the mountains. People are more likely to answer a local number, especially when they don’t recognize an out-of-area call.\"","\"Give it to me.\"","Jordan took the phone from his pocket and handed it over.","Alpha Sebastian walked to the window, turned his back to Jordan, and dialed the number he knew by heart.","Eira answered on the second ring.","\"Hello?\"","The 530 area code caught her attention.","It was a Northern California number, close enough to the mountains where the group home was located.","Sam had never owned a phone. If he needed to call her, he would have to borrow someone else’s.","That explained the unfamiliar number.","\"Sam?\" Eira’s voice softened. \"Is that you? It’s Eira. Your big sister.\"","She waited.","For nearly thirty seconds, no one spoke. Eira stayed on the line. If Sam had finally worked up the courage to call, she would not rush him.","Then a man answered.","\"Eira. It’s me.\"","Her face went still.","Alpha Sebastian.","\"Why are you calling me?\"","\"I found Sam,\" Alpha Sebastian said. \"If you want to know how he’s doing, meet me tomorrow morning.\"","Eira said nothing.","Alpha Sebastian lowered his voice. \"We’ll meet at the place where I proposed to you. Just once. I won’t keep you there.\""]},{"number":210,"title":"Chapter 210 A Blade Wrapped in Silk","paragraphs":["Eira stood outside the lab, phone pressed to her ear. Her jaw tightened.","\"What are you playing at, Sebastian?\"","\"I’m not playing at anything.\" His voice turned soft, almost pitiful. \"I just want to talk, Eira. That’s all. Can you give me a few minutes?\"","\"I received your legal notice six days ago. Very professional. Very carefully worded.\"","She leaned against the wall as engineers moved through the corridor around her.","Alpha Sebastian let out a quiet breath, as if she had wounded him. \"Did Alpha Killian help you write it? I warned you about him. He’s dangerous. Get too close, and he’ll use you until there’s nothing left.\"","\"You’re the dangerous one, Sebastian.\"","She ended the call before he could answer.","Anger burned beneath her calm expression. She took two slow breaths, squared her shoulders, and kept moving.","Her phone buzzed again.","Sebastian: Tomorrow at ten. Just you and me, Eira.","A second text followed.","Sebastian: Sam is staying with a distant relative, but it isn’t a good situation. He isn’t enrolled in school, and no one is really looking out for him. I’ve already helped arrange a place for him. We can talk about it tomorrow.","Eira read the messages twice.","The words looked harmless. The pressure behind them was not.","Alpha Sebastian had not threatened her. He did not have to. He knew she would want to know where Sam was, who he was staying with, and whether he was safe. He was counting on the fact that she could not get those answers without meeting him.","He knew exactly where to push.","Eira was one of the former residents who still came back to the group home. Some returned during the holidays. Others sent money when they could. A few vanished from the records the moment they aged out.","Eira simply kept showing up.","She brought winter coats, school supplies, grocery cards, and birthday presents. She remembered who hated thunderstorms and who needed a little extra time to answer a question. The pupstrusted her because she never treated them like charity cases.","Alpha Sebastian knew she could ignore him.","He also knew she would never ignore Sam.","Eira had always cared about the people the Packs left behind: abandoned Omegas, wolfless children, and anyone without a family name or a powerful Alpha to protect them.","In their world, an Omega pup with no bloodline could be treated as less valuable than an Alpha’s hunting dog.","Eira knew exactly what that felt like.","She had told Alpha Sebastian everything when she still believed marriage meant complete trust. She had given him her childhood, her fears, and every place where she was most vulnerable.","He had remembered all of it.","Now he was using it to pull her back.","Eira had never thought of herself as naturally gifted. She knew hard work could not always beat talent. She simply refused to let that stop her.","That stubbornness had taken her from a remote mountain town to Stanford, then to a federal lab and the Sovereign Processor Initiative.","She had never lost a class, a position, or a research opportunity.","Love was the only place where she had ever let herself lose.","She ended the call, opened her contacts, and called Miss Gwen at the group home.","Miss Gwen answered after a few rings.","\"Sweetheart, I can’t discuss Sam’s situation over the phone. We need the proper paperwork, and I can’t make exceptions. Not even for you.\"","Miss Gwen paused.","\"But you could come home a little earlier this year, couldn’t you?\"","Eira understood the message. Miss Gwen could not discuss Sam over the phone, but she was asking Eira to come back in person.","\"I’ll come home for Christmas,\" Eira said, softening her voice. \"Not just for a quick visit. I’ll stay a few days.\"","Miss Gwen’s silence warmed.","\"I’ll get your room ready. Send me your flight details, and I’ll pick you up myself.\"","\"Thank you. And please take care of yourself, okay? I have to go.\"","\"I will. Love you.\"","\"Love you too.\"","They ended the call.","The next morning, Eira was pulling on her coat when Mrs. Jones appeared with a wool scarf. Before Eira could object, she wrapped it around her neck and handed her a black umbrella.","\"The forecast says rain,\" Mrs. Jones said. \"Take the umbrella. It’s supposed to be cold and windy.\"","\"I’ll be fine.\"","\"That’s what people say right before they come home soaked and sick.\"","Mrs. Jones opened the front door. The two German shepherds waited beside it, watching Eira with sleepy concern.","Eira scratched both dogs behind the ears, then headed for the black Sterling SUV waiting at the curb.","Alpha Killian had been gone for almost a week, handling Pack business near the Sterling border.","According to Mrs. Jones, a group of rogues had crossed into Sterling territory, and several abandoned pups had been found hiding in the mountains. Alpha Killian had stayed behind to manage the border patrols and find the pups a safe place to stay.","Eira had been just as busy. She spent her days in the lab, came home after dark, and checked on the renovation at 10 Ashford Lane whenever she could.","They were both running on empty.","By the time one of them was finally free, the other was usually already asleep.","Mrs. Jones watched the SUV pull away, then texted Alpha Killian.","[When are you coming home, Alpha? Miss Eira looked upset when she got back last night. She looked even worse this morning.]","Eira rarely showed when something was bothering her, but Mrs. Jones had helped raise two generations of Sterling Alphas. She knew what pain looked like.","Alpha Killian replied within minutes.","[Wrapping things up. I’ll be home soon.]","Mrs. Jones rolled her eyes.","[Don’t text me that. Text her.]","A few minutes later, another message came through.","[Flight’s booked. I’ll be home tonight.]","Mrs. Jones smiled and slipped her phone into her pocket.","--","By the time Eira stepped out of the SUV, the sky had turned dark and gray. Cold rain drifted through the air, carried by a sharp wind. She pulled her coat tighter as she walked toward the coffee shop. Her breath came out in faint white clouds before disappearing.","The birch trees outside were bare, their thin branches scratching at the sky. Warm light spilled through the café windows, and the smell of fresh coffee reached the sidewalk every time the door opened.","This was where Alpha Sebastian had proposed.","Years earlier, Eira had come here after the Sovereign Processor Initiative was shelved. Overnight, the project she had built her career around had disappeared, and she had no idea what would come next.","With only a few crumpled bills in her wallet, she had bought a large drip coffee and taken a seat by the second-floor window. She had stared at the rain until the coffee went cold.","Then Alpha Sebastian had called.","He arrived half an hour later and found her sitting alone by the window. He did not push her to talk. He simply sat beside her and let her explain how close she was to losing her job and everything she had worked for.","When she finally ran out of words, he pulled her against his chest and lowered his mouth to her ear.","\"It’s okay.\"","A moment later, he took her hand.","\"Eira, marry me. Let me give you a home.\"","She believed him."]},{"number":211,"title":"Chapter 211 The Terms","paragraphs":["Eira pushed open the café door, and the bell above it gave a soft chime.","Only a few customers sat downstairs. A barista glanced up from the register.","\"Hi. Are you meeting someone?\"","\"Sebastian Hale.\"","The barista nodded toward the staircase. \"He’s upstairs.\"","Alpha Sebastian had reserved the entire upstairs room for the morning.","Eira climbed the stairs and found him waiting by the window, in the same corner where he had proposed four years ago.","He stood the moment he saw her.","His charcoal suit fit perfectly, his hair was neatly combed back, and a familiar smile settled across his face. He looked ready for a board meeting or a formal fundraiser.","But his lips were pale, and dark circles shadowed his eyes.","The legal notice had clearly shaken him. His stomach could not have recovered that quickly.","Two identical lattes sat on the table.","\"Eira.\" He pulled out a chair. \"Please, sit down.\"","Eira sat but left the latte untouched.","Alpha Sebastian glanced at the cup. \"You’re not going to drink it?\"","\"I don’t take anything from the Hales.\" She held his gaze. \"Isabella spiked my drink once. Or did you forget?\"","Shame flickered across his face.","He had not forgotten. Isabella had betrayed Eira. Serena had betrayed her too. And he had stood by and let both of them get away with it.","That made him just as guilty.","\"I would never do that to you.\"","\"You don’t get to ask me to trust you anymore.\"","The words hit him harder than he expected.","Eira kept her chair angled away from him. She did not touch the latte, the table, or anything else Alpha Sebastian had handled. Every small rejection scraped against his nerves.","\"Let’s cut to the chase,\" she said. \"You want me to drop my claim to the marital assets.\"","\"No.\"","\"Then why am I here?\"","Alpha Sebastian unlocked his phone and turned it toward her.","The first photo showed Sam standing outside a run-down house in an oversized coat. His cheeks were red from the cold, and the skin around his knuckles was cracked. In the second photo, he wore new clothes, but he still looked thin, tired, and wary.","\"His relatives are struggling,\" Alpha Sebastian said. \"Six people are sharing a small rental in one of the poorest border Packs. They already have three children in school. Sam wasn’t enrolled. They had him working instead.\"","Eira stared at the screen.","Two years ago, Sam had been safe at the group home. He had warm clothes, regular meals, and adults who knew how to care for him.","Now he looked completely alone.","\"I paid for a place at a boarding school,\" Alpha Sebastian continued. \"I spoke to the headmaster myself. He’ll have food, medical care, and a proper education. I also found his relatives a better place to live.\"","Eira slowly raised her eyes. \"And what do you want in return?\"","Alpha Sebastian’s silence answered her before he spoke.","\"I want us to keep the divorce private.\"","Her expression hardened.","\"\"To the business world and the Packs, we’re still together.Privately, I won’t ask you to come home or act like my wife.\"","\"You want me to pretend we’re still married.\"","\"I want time.\"","\"You want protection for your company.\"","Alpha Sebastian did not deny it.","Eira gave a cold laugh. \"And Sam is the price.\"","\"If you want to stay involved in his life, you need to keep your connection to me public.\"","\"You’re holding a child over my head and calling it a marriage.\"","\"I’m trying to make sure he’s safe.\"","\"You had two years to do that. You only found him when you needed leverage.\"","The color drained from Alpha Sebastian’s face.","Eira pushed his phone back across the table.","\"Give me the name of Sam’s school, his legal guardian, and the social worker assigned to his case. If he’s being neglected, I’ll handle it through the proper legal channels.\"","\"You won’t be able to reach him that way.\"","For the first time, Eira’s carefully controlled expression cracked.","\"There’s one more condition.\"","She turned her head slightly. \"Say it.\"","\"Come to dinner with me tonight.\"","Eira’s eyes narrowed. \"Why?\"","\"Snowmark’s lead negotiator expects me to bring my Luna. If the divorce becomes public before the deal closes, they may walk away.\"","She understood immediately.","\"So you need me to stand beside you while you close the deal.\"","\"I need you there for one night.\"","\"No. You need my name, my reputation, and the work I did for Hale Group.\"","\"That’s not what I meant.\"","\"It’s exactly what you meant.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened. \"Eira, I do care about you. I wouldn’t be asking if I had another option.\"","\"You always have another option. You just keep choosing the one that hurts me.\"","She stood, slipped on her coat, and fastened each button with steady fingers.","\"You used my work to build your company, spent our money on Serena, and now you want me to help save your deal.\"","Alpha Sebastian said nothing.","\"So this is what you call love?\"","The question stopped him cold.","She did not wait for an answer.","\"Sebastian, you make me sick.\"","\"I know,\" Alpha Sebastian said, lowering his eyes.","He had known from the moment he decided to use Sam as leverage. Whatever happened next, Eira would hate him even more.","But he felt trapped. He could not let the Hale Pack become a pawn in someone else’s power struggle. He also refused to spend the next two years silenced by a noncompete agreement.","He had been backed into a corner. One more mistake could bring everything down.","\"Eira, I don’t want things to end like this.\" He looked up at her, his expression almost pleading. \"Can’t you give me a little more time? Just out of respect for what we had?\"","She stared at him.","\"When you were sleeping with Serena, were you showing any respect for our marriage?\"","Alpha Sebastian had no answer.","Eira picked up her coat and walked out.","\"Six-thirty tonight,\" he called after her. \"I’ll pick you up at Number Nine.\"","She did not turn around.","Alpha Sebastian watched her disappear down the stairs. He knew she would come, but not because she still cared about him.","She would come for Sam."]},{"number":212,"title":"Chapter 212 Play the Long Game","paragraphs":["Outside, Eira climbed into the waiting SUV. She took a long drink of water, then pulled out her phone.","The recording was still running.","She stopped it and sent the file to a group chat titled Case Prep. The members were Eira, Alpha Killian, Susan, and Miles.","Alpha Killian had created the chat before she entered the café. His only instruction had been simple.","Record everything.","That was why Eira had kept her temper under control. She had not walked away with a public argument. She had walked away with a recording, several useful admissions, and a clearer picture of Alpha Sebastian’s plan.","Miles replied first. A document appeared in the chat.","Miles: The recording is transcribed. I flagged the key points. Review it when you can.","A second message followed.","Miles: Beta Jordan has been out of contact for two weeks. He’s probably the one handling Sam’s situation near the Klamath territory.","Susan replied a moment later.","Susan: A minor’s name change can move quickly when the legal guardian requests it, especially in a remote Pack. If Sam is over fifteen, we may have about a week to challenge it. If he’s younger, the paperwork may already be complete.","Eira started typing, then deleted the message.","She tried again.","Eira: The lawsuit can wait. Finding Sam comes first. This is not over.","Susan: Understood. I’ll look into emergency relief and temporary guardianship options.","Another message appeared.","Killian: Snowmark’s regional lead is Soren. He hasn’t met Natalie yet. Have her go with you tonight.","Miles replied almost immediately.","Miles: I’ll drive.","The plan came together in less than a minute. Dinner with Soren. Miles on transportation. Susan working on the legal route. Alpha Killian handling the Pack side.","For the first time since Alpha Sebastian mentioned Sam, the tightness in Eira’s chest began to ease.","Alpha Sebastian had tried to isolate her by hiding the boy behind new paperwork, a new address, and a family she could not reach.","He had forgotten one thing.","Eira was no longer facing him alone.","Her phone buzzed again. This time, the message was private.","Killian: I’m flying back to the Bay Area tonight.","Eira stared at the screen.","The words felt strangely familiar. Alpha Sebastian had once promised to come home in almost the same way.","She typed a reply, deleted it, then tried again.","Eira: What time do you land?","Killian: 10:10 p.m. SFO. International Terminal.","Eira checked the time. By the time Alpha Killian cleared customs, picked up his luggage, and drove from San Francisco to Palo Alto, it would be close to midnight.","He had probably eaten on the flight, but she knew he would still be exhausted and hungry after the long trip.","She drove back to Southridge and found Mrs. Jones in the kitchen.","\"Could you prepare something for Killian?\" Eira asked. \"He’ll be getting back late tonight. Please have it sent over to Number One.\"","Mrs. Jones’s face lit up.","\"Alpha Killian is coming home?\"","\"After ten. He’ll probably be exhausted by the time he gets here.\"","\"I’ll make something warm and easy to reheat. What about you?\"","\"I’m not sure when I’ll be back. I have plans tonight.\"","Mrs. Jones paused. \"Plans?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"At this hour?\" Her expression tightened. \"Where are Miles and Natalie?\"","\"They’re coming with me.\"","\"And with Alpha Killian still out of town, you shouldn’t be going anywhere without backup. Especially after dark.\"","\"It isn’t Sterling business.\"","Mrs. Jones studied her face. Eira was clearly leaving something out, but Mrs. Jones knew better than to push when she used that tone.","\"All right,\" she said. \"I’ll send his dinner over and keep a plate here for you, just in case.\"","\"That would be great. Thank you.\"","\"Keep your phone on.\"","\"I will.\"","Eira went upstairs to change.","She did not dress for a date. She chose a black silk blouse, a fitted charcoal blazer, and tailored trousers that fell neatly over her heels. The outfit was polished and professional without looking flashy. She finished with a slim gold watch and a pair of small pearl earrings.","She wasn’t going to the dinner as Alpha Sebastian’s Luna. She was going as the renowned Dr. Crawford.","--","At six, a black SUV pulled up outside the Number Nine gate.","Miles was behind the wheel. Natalie sat in the passenger seat wearing a navy pantsuit, low heels, and a discreet Sterling Group pin tucked inside her blazer. She looked like a sharp executive assistant, not a security escort.","That was exactly the point.","Natalie held out a paper coffee cup. \"I got you a black coffee. No sugar.\"","\"Thanks.\"","Eira took the cup.","Natalie gave her outfit a quick once-over. \"Very Dr. Crawford. Very untouchable.\"","\"That’s the goal.\"","Natalie took a sip from her own coffee. \"Tonight, I’m your assistant. I’ll manage your schedule, keep Alpha Sebastian from cornering you, and cut off anyone who tries to get you drunk.\"","\"I doubt anyone will try that.\"","\"People with expensive watches and bad intentions always think they’re charming.\"","Miles adjusted his glasses and glanced at them through the rearview mirror.","\"While you’re there, get Soren’s direct contact information. Not his assistant’s number. His personal business line.\"","Eira nodded. \"I’ll handle it.\"","The Snowmark project was expected to run for months, possibly years. Their search for Sam could not wait that long.","If Snowmark learned that Alpha Sebastian had hidden the divorce while using Eira’s name to secure the partnership, Soren and the rest of the executive team would be furious.","They had not agreed to be dragged into a private marital scandal or used as part of Alpha Sebastian’s cover story.","Whether the Snowmark deal could survive the evening was another question entirely."]},{"number":213,"title":"Chapter 213 The Woman Who Outshines Him","paragraphs":["At 6:20 p.m., Eira texted Alpha Sebastian first.","Eira: I’m at the Southridge gate.","Alpha Sebastian pulled up a few minutes later. A black Sterling SUV was waiting by the entrance, and he knew exactly where she was.","His jaw tightened.","He got out, crossed the driveway, and tapped on the rear passenger window. Both windows lowered at once.","Eira sat in the back beside Natalie. Miles was behind the wheel. They looked less like a private car service and more like a security detail.","Alpha Killian was still overseas, but his people had made sure Eira was not traveling alone.","\"Eira,\" Alpha Sebastian said, forcing a smile. \"I bought you a car. Once you pass your driving test, you won’t have to keep borrowing rides from other Packs.\"","Natalie placed a hand against her chest.","\"Oh, Alpha Sebastian. Dr. Crawford is one of Sterling’s most valuable partners. When someone that important needs a ride, Alpha Killian sends a car.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s smile faded.","Natalie continued in a pleasant tone. \"Besides, Dr. Crawford barely has time to sleep, let alone sit through a driving test.\"","She gave him a polite smile.","\"Some people understand how to hold on to good talent. Others are still learning.\"","Alpha Sebastian ignored the jab and reached for the rear door handle.","\"Eira, get in my car.\"","The door did not open.","Miles smiled through the window. \"That ride is a little basic for someone of Dr. Crawford’s standing, Alpha Sebastian. Sterling takes care of its own.\"","Natalie nodded. \"There’s no reason to charge transportation to Hale Group. Alpha Killian has the resources, and he does not mind spending them on people who matter.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s expression darkened.","Eira watched him with the faintest hint of amusement.","That small smile stung more than anything Natalie had said.","\"Married couples usually don’t show up in separate cars,\" Alpha Sebastian muttered.","Eira looked at him through the open window. \"Some do. Especially couples who have already signed the divorce papers but still have to put on a show for everyone else.\"","Her gaze moved over him, cool and unimpressed.","\"And separate cars never bothered you during our marriage.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened.","Eira turned to Miles. \"Where are we headed?\"","\"Snowmark’s reception is at the Fairmont,\" he said.","\"Then lead the way. I’m not spending all night in the driveway.\"","Alpha Sebastian had expected to find a woman he could pressure into following his rules. Instead, Eira looked completely out of his reach.","His hands curled at his sides. After a moment, he turned away, got into his own car, and pulled out ahead of them.","Eira settled into the back seat and opened her phone. She searched for the earliest flight to the Klamath area the next morning.","Miss Gwen’s careful warning was too important to ignore.","Natalie noticed the booking screen. \"Where are you going?\"","Eira trusted both of them. \"Klamath.\"","Miles glanced at her in the rearview mirror. \"You’re following the lead on Sam?\"","She nodded.","\"You could wait until Alpha Killian gets back,\" Miles said. \"He can send a team with you.\"","\"I’m not waiting.\"","Natalie leaned closer to look at the screen. \"Sterling has a satellite office near Klamath. Book the trip through the company. We’ll cover the flight, the hotel, and local transportation.\"","\"This is personal.\"","\"It’s a rescue operation involving a vulnerable pup,\" Natalie said. \"Sterling has always helped people who don’t have anyone else in their corner.\"","Miles nodded. \"We’ll arrange a driver and a secure place for you to stay. Someone familiar with the local territory can go with you.\"","\"You don’t have to do all that.\"","\"Actually, we do,\" Natalie said. \"Travel arrangements are part of my job. I book flights, reserve hotels, and make sure people don’t get stranded in unfamiliar territory. We’re not sending you into the mountains alone.\"","Eira looked down at her phone.","The earliest flight was almost full. Before she could refresh the page, Natalie had already opened another booking site.","\"Don’t worry,\" Natalie said. \"You’re not sleeping in an airport or fighting over the last rental car. I’ll take care of it.\"","--","They reached the hotel at 7:10 p.m. Alpha Sebastian was waiting outside the entrance.","Snowmark handled business the American way. There were no formal toasts and no banquet tables piled high with food. Tonight’s event was a private cocktail reception. The guests were there to network, build trust, and talk business. Servers moved through the room with champagne, wine, and small plates of crab cakes, shrimp skewers, and mini beef sliders.","When Eira stepped out of the SUV, Alpha Sebastian finally noticed what she was wearing.","Her black silk blouse and fitted charcoal blazer gave her a polished, professional look. Her tailored trousers fell neatly over her heels, while a slim gold watch and small pearl earrings completed the understated outfit.","It was not the formal look he had expected.","On anyone else, the outfit might have looked simple. On Eira, it made her look completely out of his reach.","Alpha Sebastian frowned, then forced himself to let it go. She had come. For now, that was all that mattered.","Miles handed the keys to the valet and joined them. Natalie fell into step beside Eira.","Alpha Sebastian’s expression soured. \"She’s coming in with us?\"","\"I’m Dr. Crawford’s assistant,\" Natalie replied.","She was not only Eira’s assistant, and Alpha Sebastian knew it. Natalie worked for Sterling Group. If he challenged her presence, he would have to explain why Sterling’s staff was protecting his wife.","He kept his mouth shut.","Eira was already heading toward the hotel entrance with Natalie beside her.","\"Are you coming?\" she asked without looking back. \"We’re not standing out here all night.\"","Alpha Sebastian followed them inside.","The lobby smelled of polished wood, citrus, and expensive perfume. Guests in tailored suits and cocktail dresses moved between the bar and the reception area. A server passed with a tray of champagne and bite-sized crab cakes.","As they stepped into the elevator, Alpha Sebastian moved closer to Eira.","\"We’re still husband and wife tonight,\" he said quietly. \"You should be walking in with me.\"","Eira pressed the button for the reception floor.","\"That was never really your habit,\" she said. \"Don’t start pretending now.\"","The elevator doors opened.","Eira stepped out first. A hotel attendant approached with a guest list, but Soren spotted them from across the room and came over with a drink in hand.","\"Alpha Sebastian Hale,\" he said warmly. Then his attention shifted to the two women. \"Which one is Luna Hale?\"","Sebastian reached toward Eira, but she moved first.","She extended her hand to Soren. \"I’m Dr. Crawford. Please call me Eira. And this is Natalie, my assistant.\"","Soren shook her hand. \"Of course. My apologies, Eira. I shouldn’t have assumed.\"","\"You’re fine.\"","\"And you look perfect for tonight,\" he added, glancing at her outfit.","A small smile touched Eira’s lips. \"I’m glad I got the dress code right.\"","\"You did. Please, come in.\" Soren stepped aside. \"Alpha Sebastian, you’re welcome to join us. Natalie, you too.\"","Natalie gave him a polite nod.","Soren’s warmth toward Eira was immediate and genuine. He had already decided that building a direct relationship with Eira would benefit Snowmark, whether or not she remained involved in the joint project.","Within minutes, Eira became the center of attention.","She did not flatter anyone or compete for the spotlight. She simply answered questions with calm confidence, and people naturally gathered around her. Executives introduced themselves. Investors asked about the processor design. Even guests who had never heard her speak before watched her with open interest.","Eira looked more at ease than Alpha Sebastian had seen her in years."]},{"number":214,"title":"Chapter 214 The Birthday Trap","paragraphs":["Natalie leaned toward Alpha Sebastian, wearing a pleasant smile for anyone watching.","\"Do you see how easily she commands a room now?\"","Alpha Sebastian’s face darkened.","Natalie took a sip of sparkling water and lowered her voice.","\"It’s almost like she was never the problem.\"","Alpha Sebastian said nothing.","\"She only started to shine once she stepped out of your shadow,\" Natalie added. \"That has to sting a little.\"","His expression hardened.","Natalie smiled into her glass. \"Relax, Alpha Sebastian. We’re only here for the reception.\"","\"Natalie, watch your tone,\" Alpha Sebastian said quietly. The warning in his voice was unmistakable. \"Who gave you the right to speak to me like that?\"","\"Alpha Killian did,\" Natalie replied without blinking.","She had stood beside Alpha Killian through boardroom fights with Alphas far more intimidating than Sebastian Hale.","A few sharp words from a second-tier Pack leader were not enough to rattle her. Whatever trouble she got into, Alpha Killian always had her back.","It helped knowing someone powerful was in your corner.","\"Alpha Killian was very clear,\" Natalie continued, her voice calm and professional. \"His executive staff speak for him, and our statements carry his authority. That means we choose our words carefully. We don’t make accusations without proof, and we don’t insult people without a reason.\"","\"If you disagree with me, Alpha Sebastian, you’re welcome to call him and ask.\"","Alpha Sebastian had nothing to say. Anything he said would only draw more attention to the exchange.","His expression hardened as he turned away, looking for Eira.","Across the room, Eira had just finished making small talk with a few business guests. She was already checking her phone.","A message from Miss Gwen had come through. It included a livestream from the Klamath Mountains, where the first snow of the season had begun to fall over the group home.","Beneath the link were several birthday messages.","[Happy birthday, sweetheart. I hope this year brings you peace and plenty of good things.]","Miss Gwen had also attached photos of handmade cards from the children. The cards were covered in crooked handwriting, bright stickers, glitter, and uneven drawings of wolves, mountains, and birthday cakes.","One showed a gray wolf wearing a crooked crown.","[Happy birthday, Big Sister Eira!]","Another said:","[We miss you. Come home soon.]","Warmth spread through Eira’s chest. She smiled before she could stop herself.","\"Who’s got you smiling like that?\"","Alpha Sebastian had returned without her noticing. His voice was soft, almost familiar.","Eira locked her phone and stepped away from him.","His brow furrowed. \"You don’t have to act like I’m a stranger. I’d like us to be able to talk the way we used to.\"","\"That was before.\"","\"Before what?\"","\"Before you became my ex-husband.\"","Alpha Sebastian glanced around the room to see whether anyone from Snowmark had heard her.","\"Stop trying to provoke me,\" he muttered.","He looked frustrated, but there was something else in his expression too. He carried himself like the injured party, as if every choice he had made had been forced on him.","Eira met his eyes.","\"Sebastian, everything about tonight was your choice. So who are you trying to fool with the wounded act?\"","Before he could answer, Soren approached with a fresh drink in hand.","\"Alpha Sebastian. Eira.\" He gestured toward the open space near the center of the room. \"The band is about to start. Would you two like to dance?\"","His gaze moved between them.","They looked perfectly matched on paper. Alpha Sebastian was polished and controlled. Eira was elegant, confident, and impossible to overlook.","Soren found himself wondering whether they still looked as natural together on the dance floor as they did in photographs.","Before Eira could answer, Alpha Sebastian reached for her hand.","\"Of course,\" he said.","Eira stepped back. Natalie moved between them with practiced ease.","\"Eira’s not much of a dancer. \" she said. \"Sorry, Mr. Soren.\"","Only Soren seemed to believe her.","He looked genuinely disappointed, then turned to Alpha Sebastian with an encouraging smile. \"You should teach her sometime, Alpha Sebastian. Even if it’s just at home on a quiet night. Nothing beats dancing with your mate in the kitchen.\"","Alpha Sebastian took the hint and held out his hand again.","\"I can teach you right now.\"","\"Gross,\" Eira said.","When he only stared at her, she added, \"You’re gross.\"","Soren froze. His blue eyes moved between them.","Natalie stepped in with an easy smile. \"Sorry, Soren. They’re having a little marital spat. Nothing serious. Long-term couples can be like that. They argue because they care.\"","Soren nodded, relieved to have an explanation. \"Of course. I understand.\"","Alpha Sebastian knew better.","Eira had not called him gross out of affection. She had meant every word.","Soren turned to Natalie instead. \"Would you care to dance?\"","\"That’s sweet of you, but I’ll pass,\" Natalie said politely.","There was no chance she was leaving Eira alone with Alpha Sebastian, not even for one song.","\"I’m getting a little tired,\" Eira said. \"Would it be all right if I stepped outside for some air?\"","\"Of course.\"","She pulled out her phone. \"Before I go, could I get your direct number?\"","\"Absolutely.\"","Soren handed her his phone at once, clearly pleased that she had asked. Eira entered her number, gave him a missed call, and saved his contact before returning the phone.","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened.","By the time he stepped forward, the exchange was already over.","\"Let’s go,\" Eira told Natalie.","The two women turned toward the exit.","Alpha Sebastian watched them walk away. Eira’s posture was calm, and Natalie stayed close beside her, blocking him from following too closely. He stood there, surrounded by music and polite conversation, while the woman he had once considered his wife walked out of his reach.","Then a mind-link opened in his head.","Beta Jordan’s voice came through, low and urgent.","[Alpha, the first snow has started in the Klamath Mountains.]","Alpha Sebastian’s attention sharpened.","The first snow meant one thing.","Eira’s birthday.","An idea came to him.","\"Wait,\" he called.","Eira stopped and slowly turned around.","Alpha Sebastian faced Soren.","\"It’s Eira’s birthday today,\" he said. \"How about I play something for her before she leaves? Maybe we can get everyone to sing ...Happy Birthday.’\"","Soren’s face brightened.\"Absolutely.\"","He clapped twice to get the room’s attention. The conversations faded, and guests turned toward him.","\"Everyone, may I have your attention?\" Soren announced. \"It’s Dr. Crawford’s birthday tonight.\"","Warm congratulations rose from the crowd.","A staff member quickly rolled the piano toward the center of the room. Servers paused with trays in their hands, and several executives gathered around with smiles that were friendly, curious, or simply eager to watch the Hale family drama unfold.","Eira glanced toward the exit. Leaving now would only draw attention.","She turned back to Alpha Sebastian.","He smiled as if he had done her a favor.","Her look said it all.","What a snake."]},{"number":215,"title":"Chapter 215 The Price of Sam","paragraphs":["\"Happy birthday, Eira,\" Alpha Sebastian said softly, wearing the same warm, wounded smile.","Natalie turned sharply. \"Wait. Today’s your birthday?\"","Eira’s expression softened when she looked at her. \"It is.\"","Natalie understood at once. Alpha Sebastian had turned the entire reception into a performance so Eira could not leave without exposing their divorce. He had betrayed her, wasted four years of her loyalty, and still thought a public display would win him another chance.","What an idiot.","Natalie stepped in front of Eira, blocking Alpha Sebastian’s view of her.","A staff member rolled the piano into the center of the room. Alpha Sebastian handed his drink to a passing server and sat down. He placed his fingers on the keys, then looked at Eira with an expression full of carefully rehearsed devotion.","\"This was the song playing the night I proposed to my wife,\" he told the guests. \"We even went back to that café yesterday. And today happens to be her birthday.\"","He smiled at Eira.","\"Happy birthday, sweetheart.\"","Eira’s expression did not change.","Natalie leaned toward her. \"He should’ve gone into acting. Instead, he’s making this everyone’s problem.\"","\"There’s a reason he and Serena get along so well,\" Eira murmured.","Natalie glanced at her. \"Why?\"","\"They both make a living pretending.\"","Natalie nodded. \"Fair point.\"","Eira had never heard Alpha Sebastian play the piano, and she had no interest in listening now. To her, the performance was nothing more than another sales pitch for Snowmark’s executives.","She glanced down at her phone, where Miss Gwen had been sending her messages from the children.","It was her birthday after all. Maybe she should do something small to celebrate.","She opened a delivery app and ordered three small cakes from a nearby bakery. One was a spice cake for herself and Mrs. Jones. The other two were for Natalie and Miles.","Alpha Sebastian noticed that she was not watching him. She was focused on her phone instead, and his jaw tightened.","The song ended, and the room applauded. Eira looked up just long enough to acknowledge him before returning her attention to her phone.","Then the pianist began the opening notes of \"Happy Birthday.\"","The guests joined in, smiling as they sang. Eira put away her phone and smiled at the room. If Alpha Sebastian had not arranged the whole spectacle, she might have enjoyed it.","When the song ended, Soren raised his glass.","\"Happy birthday, Dr. Crawford!\"","The guests echoed him.","\"Thank you,\" Eira said.","Alpha Sebastian stood and crossed the room. The crowd parted to let him through.","\"Happy birthday, Eira,\" he said, looking polished, heartbroken, and far too pleased with himself.","She did not even nod.","Then someone near the back called out, \"Kiss her!\"","A few guests laughed. Others quickly joined in.","\"Kiss! Kiss! Kiss!\"","Alpha Sebastian smiled as if the crowd had handed him exactly what he wanted. He stepped closer.","Natalie’s instincts went on high alert. She could not stop him without making the situation look suspicious. Eira still needed information about Sam, and Snowmark had not yet realized that Alpha Sebastian was using the reception to cover up his divorce.","Natalie silently wished Alpha Killian were there. No one would dare pressure Eira into kissing Alpha Sebastian if Alpha Killian stood beside her.","Then Eira smiled.","\"Sure,\" she said.","Alpha Sebastian’s eyes brightened.","Eira held out her hand.","\"But first, transfer the $118 million in research funding you promised me. A deal’s a deal.\"","The room fell silent.","Everyone assumed she was talking about some private research agreement. Only Alpha Sebastian knew what the money really represented. It was the marital property he had transferred to Serena.","If he could put her on the spot in front of a room full of people, she could do the same to him.","To everyone else, it looked like playful flirting. Eira was smiling, and she clearly had the upper hand.","Alpha Sebastian could not kiss her.","More importantly, he could not afford the $118 million she had just demanded.","The tension in Natalie’s chest eased. Thank God. Eira could handle herself.","Natalie stepped in with a bright smile.","\"That’s right, Alpha Sebastian. You promised her a birthday gift.\"","Her tone made it sound like harmless teasing between a married couple. But Natalie knew the truth. Alpha Sebastian did not have that kind of cash available.","He had not expected Eira to name the amount in front of Snowmark’s executives. No one else understood what it meant, but he did.","His carefully planned evening had blown up in his face.","He forced out a laugh. \"My wife is joking. Don’t encourage her. Thank you all for the birthday wishes.\"","Eira thanked the guests as well, then turned to Soren.","\"I’m getting tired. I should head home.\"","\"Of course,\" Soren said warmly. \"Enjoy the rest of your birthday.\"","Eira glanced at Alpha Sebastian. \" Soren is one of Snowmark’s most important partners. You should stay and give him your full attention.\"","Alpha Sebastian could not walk out on Snowmark’s director without raising questions. Still, he followed her toward the exit.","Soren had no reason to stop a husband from seeing his wife out.","The ballroom doors closed behind them, cutting off the music and conversation.","Alpha Sebastian turned to her. \"You said you’d stay for the whole evening.\"","\"I agreed to help you make an appearance. I never promised to stay until midnight.\"","\"Eira, business relationships are supposed to be handled properly.\"","She stopped and faced him.","\"Don’t lecture me about commitment. You married me, ran around with Serena, and spent our money on her. You refused to acknowledge our bond in public, dragged out the divorce, and then chased me only when you needed something.\"","His face went pale.","\"You brought me here to play happy wife for Snowmark,\" she continued. \"They believed the act, and they let me leave. Your cover story worked. We’re done.\"","She turned toward the elevators.","Alpha Sebastian moved after her. He could not waste the first real chance he had gotten to speak with her in weeks.","\"Don’t you want to talk to Sam?\"","Eira stopped.","\"Stay a little longer,\" he said quickly. \"I’ll call his school and arrange a conversation. You can hear his voice tonight.\"","She looked back at him.","Alpha Sebastian mistook the hesitation in her eyes for hope and softened his voice.","\"Eira, you haven’t seen Sam in two years. Don’t you want to know how he’s doing?\""]},{"number":216,"title":"Chapter 216 The Legal Notice","paragraphs":["\"No,\" Eira said.","This time, she did not look back.","It was not that she did not want to hear Sam’s voice. She wanted to more than anything. But if Sam heard her through Alpha Sebastian’s phone, he might believe the lie even more.","Natalie walked beside her, smart enough not to ask questions.","The revolving doors opened onto a cold, rainy night. Miles waited at the curb beneath a wide black umbrella, the town car idling nearby.","Eira slipped into the back seat and lowered the window a few inches. Cool rain misted her face before she rolled it back up.","Miles turned on the heat.","\"Are we heading straight back to Southridge, or do you want to make a quick stop?\" he asked.","\"Cake first.\"","Natalie grinned. \"Now that sounds like a birthday plan.\"","Then she paused. \"Wait. Is today actually your birthday? Alpha Sebastian made it sound like some grand romantic surprise.\"","\"Not according to my birth certificate.\" Eira watched the rain slide down the window. \"I celebrate on the day of the first snow in the Klamath Mountains.\"","Natalie opened her mouth to reply, but Eira’s phone rang.","The caller ID showed Beatrice.","\"Eira, sweetheart, are you free tomorrow?\" Beatrice asked. \"I feel like I haven’t seen you in forever. Are you buried in work again?\"","\"I’m free. I have to leave for the airport in the afternoon, though.\"","\"Of course you do. You always have somewhere to be.\"","\"I’m trying to slow down.\"","\"Sure you are.\" Beatrice paused. \"I’ll have the kitchen make your favorite dishes tomorrow. You’re staying for lunch. We’ll celebrate your birthday before you leave.\"","Eira blinked. \"How did you know?\"","\"Alaric told me. He figured it out the year before he died. He said he’d seen you buy one of those little triangular mousse cakes whenever the first snow came to Klamath.\"","Eira’s lips curved.\"I’ll come by first thing tomorrow.\"","\"Good. I’ll see you then. And don’t skip breakfast.\"","\"I won’t.\"","\"Eira.\"","She sighed. \"I’ll eat breakfast.\"","\"That’s better. Good night, sweetheart.\"","\"Good night, Beatrice .\"","The call ended.","A little after eight-thirty, Miles pulled into a bakery that was still open. He returned with the cakes Eira had ordered and handed Natalie her box.","\"Eat it,\" he said, giving her a serious look. \"Don’t post it, and don’t let Alpha Killian spot strawberries on your social media.\"","Natalie blinked. \"You’re worried he’ll find out I ate cake?\"","\"I’m worried he’ll decide you’re ignoring your nutrition plan again.\"","Natalie tucked the box against her chest. \"It’s one piece of cake.\"","\"You said that about the last three.\"","She sighed. \"Fine. I’ll eat it in private like a criminal.\"","Eira glanced at her. \"You’re being dramatic.\"","\"You’ve never seen Alpha Killian react to a bad nutrition report.\"","Miles pulled away from the curb. \"You two are impossible.\"","They dropped Natalie off first. By the time Miles pulled up outside Southridge Estates, it was a little after nine.","\"Alpha Killian lands at ten,\" he said. \"I’m heading to SFO to pick him up.\"","Eira studied him for a moment.","\"Drive safe.\"","\"I will. Try to get some sleep.\"","\"I’ll try.\"","Miles smiled, then drove away.","--","Mrs. Jones looked up as Eira came through the door with several bakery boxes.","\"You brought dessert?\"","\"Just a few cakes.\"","Mrs. Jones took one of the boxes and peeked inside. A small plaque on the lid read Happy Birthday, Eira.","She looked up. \"Wait. Is it your birthday?\"","\"Apparently.\"","\"Apparently?\" Mrs. Jones repeated. \"You’re the birthday girl, and that’s all you’ve got?\"","\"I wasn’t planning on making a big deal out of it.\"","\"Too late.\" Mrs. Jones took another box from her. \"Come on. Help me set the table.\"","\"Mrs. Jones, you really don’t have to do all that. We’re not going to finish everything.\"","\"I already made dinner. You’re eating it.\"","\"Something light, please.\"","\"There’s chicken, pasta, and vegetables. I’m not letting you live on cake.\"","\"I wasn’t planning to.\"","\"Good. Then we agree.\"","Mrs. Jones carried the boxes toward the kitchen, then stopped.","\"Lila needs to come over.\"","\"She’s probably still at the lab.\"","\"Then I’ll call her.\"","\"I can call her.\"","Mrs. Jones pulled out her phone. \"I have her number, sweetheart. I can handle this.\"","Before Eira could argue, the call connected.","\"Mrs. Jones?\" Lila answered, sounding exhausted. \"Why are you calling me this late?\"","\"You sound awful.\"","\"I feel awful. My advisor has me running another round of tests.\"","\"How much longer?\"","\"Ten minutes. Maybe fifteen if he finds another problem to throw at me.\"","\"Come to Southridge when you’re done.\"","\"Why?\"","\"It’s Eira’s birthday.\"","There was a beat of silence.","\"Wait. Today?\"","\"That’s usually how birthdays work.\"","\"Why didn’t anyone tell me?\"","\"I’m telling you now.\"","\"I’m coming.\"","\"You don’t have to rush.\"","\"I’m not rushing. I’m done for tonight. My dissertation’s approved. The lab can survive without me until morning.\"","\"Bring a coat.\"","\"I’ll be there. Save me some cake.\"","\"Your piece is already waiting.\"","\"Mrs. Jones, you’re my favorite person.\"","\"You say that every time I feed you.\"","\"And I mean it every time.\"","The call ended.","Eira laughed softly. \"She’s really coming?\"","\"She’ll be here before we cut the cake.\"","\"Then I’ll wait.\"","--","Across town, Alpha Sebastian watched Soren’s car disappear into traffic before getting into his own.","Jordan was still stuck at the office, so Alpha Sebastian had to drive himself. He had barely pulled away from the curb when Serena started calling.","Once. Twice. Again.","His phone kept lighting up until he finally answered, more annoyed than concerned.","\"Sebastian, Eira sent me a legal notice.\" Serena sounded close to panic. \"She had it delivered to my grandfather’s estate. He opened it himself and sent a car for me. Sebastian, that money was the investment you gave me, right?\"","\"You know exactly what that money was.\"","\"I’m not worried about myself.\" Her voice grew shakier. \"But if this goes to court, it could ruin your career and damage your standing with the Pack. What happens to your position as Alpha?\"","Alpha Sebastian frowned.","Something about her tone felt off. She sounded less worried about him than she did about saving herself.","\"Even if you don’t care what happens to me, think about your future,\" Serena continued, softening her voice. \"Think about our baby. You can’t let this become public.\"","That made him even more suspicious.","\"Eira sent me a notice too,\" he said. \"She wants the full amount repaid within ten days.\"","Serena went silent.","\"Six days are already gone,\" Sebastian continued. \"That leaves us four days to come up with the money.\"","Her breathing changed.","Four days.","Was Eira out of her mind?","Ten days was an aggressive deadline for a demand of this size. It left them barely enough time to respond, let alone liquidate assets, move funds, and come up with more than a hundred million dollars.","And if Eira planned to take them to court, why give them any warning at all?","\"Sebastian,\" Serena said carefully, \"you have to do something.\"","\"I’m working on it.\"","\"No. You need to fix this before my grandfather gets involved.\"","\"Your grandfather is already involved.\"","The line went quiet again.","Alpha Sebastian ended the call and tightened his grip on the steering wheel. He had no idea what Eira was planning, but she had chosen her target carefully.","She had not sent the notice to Serena’s apartment or her office. She had sent it straight to the Winthrop estate, where the family patriarch would see it before Serena had a chance to hide it."]},{"number":217,"title":"Chapter 217 How Much Have You Hidden","paragraphs":["One Hour Earlier","The Winthrop Estate","After dinner, Alpha Victor took a slow walk through the mansion’s grand hall. Rain tapped against the tall windows, and the warm chandelier light reflected off the polished marble floor.","As he passed the front hall, he heard the housekeeper muttering under her breath.","\"Miss Serena’s envelope has been sitting here for a week. She still hasn’t come by. She used to visit every other day.\"","Alpha Victor had noticed Serena’s absence as well. She had been unusually quiet lately, which was completely out of character for her.","\"What envelope?\" he asked.","The housekeeper turned. \"A legal envelope, Alpha. I don’t know what’s inside.\"","Alpha Victor held out his hand. \"Bring it to me.\"","She hurried over and placed the envelope in his palm.","It was plain and unmarked. Alpha Victor tore it open and pulled out three neatly printed pages.","The words at the top stopped him cold.","LEGAL NOTICE","The notice had been sent by Eira Crawford through Boreal & Vance, Attorneys at Law. It demanded the full return of the marital assets Serena had received from Eira and Sebastian Hale.","The amount exceeded one hundred million dollars.","Alpha Victor’s vision blurred. He swayed, and the housekeeper quickly caught his arm. Her face drained of color when she saw the letterhead.","\"Alpha, please sit down. I’ll call your doctor.\"","\"No doctor.\" Alpha Victor steadied himself against the back of a chair. His hand trembled around the papers. \"Call the driver. Bring Serena here. Now.\"","\"Alpha, your blood pressure...\"","\"Now.\"","His voice echoed through the mansion.","Marcus and Olivia stepped out of the adjoining sitting room. Alpha Victor pressed the legal notice against his chest and walked toward his study.","\"When Serena gets here, send her straight in.\"","\"Yes, Alpha,\" the housekeeper said.","Alpha Victor disappeared behind the study doors.","Marcus watched him go. \"One of these days, Serena is going to bring this whole family down with her.\"","Olivia folded her arms. \"And whose fault is that? If our son had half her common sense, your father wouldn’t have put all his faith in Serena.\"","\"So this is my fault now?\"","\"Who else’s would it be?\" Olivia shot back. \"All that family prestige doesn’t pay the bills. We built half of what we have ourselves.\"","\"Father has money.\"","\"Money he keeps locked away as if he plans to take it with him.\"","Marcus gave her a tired look. \"He doesn’t spend it.\"","Olivia fell silent.","They both knew Alpha Victor would rather watch the family struggle than touch the fortune he had spent a lifetime building.","Twenty minutes later, Serena stepped through the front door and brushed the rain from her coat. She gave Marcus and Olivia a polite nod.","Olivia pointed toward the hallway.","\"He’s in the study.\"","Serena’s stomach tightened. The housekeeper had warned her over the phone, and the driver had said Alpha Victor looked worse than he had the last time she had seen him.","She glanced at the closed study doors, took a breath, and went inside.","Alpha Victor stood behind his desk with the legal notice in his hand. Before Serena could speak, he threw the papers across the room.","She caught them against her chest.","\"Read it,\" he said. \"Then tell me what the hell this is.\"","Serena looked down at the first page. Her face went pale.","\"Grandfather, I’m sorry, but I swear I didn’t know.\" She looked up quickly. \"When I came home, I didn’t know Sebastian was married. He told me the marriage was temporary and that the divorce was already being handled.\"","Alpha Victor’s eyes narrowed. \"And the three hundred thousand dollars he sent you every month?\"","\"He called it a private investment.\"","\"It wasn’t.\"","Serena said nothing.","\"Eira’s attorneys traced the money back to joint accounts and assets held jointly by Sebastian and Eira. The monthly payments were only part of it. The penthouse, the cars, the jewelry, and the investment accounts are all listed here.\"","His voice rose.","\"The total is over one hundred million dollars.\"","\"I never asked him for any of that.\"","\"But you accepted it.\"","\"I thought he was giving it to me.\"","\"You thought a married man was giving you over a hundred million dollars out of love?\"","Serena’s face tightened. \"I didn’t know he was married when I first came home. He told me Eira was only his wife on paper. He said he was going to end it.\"","The truth was less flattering. Serena had chosen to believe Alpha Sebastian because believing him was easier than admitting she had become involved with a married Alpha.","Alpha Victor stared at her.","\"You told me Sebastian married Eira to lure you back.\"","\"I found that out later,\" Serena said quickly. \"Grandfather, this is Eira’s doing. She has always resented me. She has always hated you too. She is trying to punish me by dragging the whole family into this.\"","\"Serena!\"","Alpha Victor’s roar shook the windows.","\"How much have you kept from me? Do you have any idea what this notice means? If Eira files suit, every transfer will be examined. The accounts, the property records, the purchase contracts. Everything.\"","Serena’s lips parted, but no answer came.","\"If Sebastian loved you,\" Alpha Victor continued, \"why didn’t he make you his mate? Why didn’t he mark you? Why didn’t he claim you in front of the Pack?\"","Serena’s face burned. Angry tears filled her eyes.","\"That’s his problem. Yelling at me won’t fix it.\"","For once, Alpha Victor did not soften.","\"How many times did I tell you to walk away from Sebastian Hale? I told you to build a future with Vincent Crawford and form an alliance with the Crawford Pack. Did you hear a word I said?\"","Serena looked away.","Alpha Victor knew how the research world worked. Talent could get someone through the door, but talent alone would not keep them there. A successful career required timing, funding, connections, and the nerve to take an opportunity before someone else did.","He had spent years clearing a path for Serena. With Vincent Crawford at her side, the Crawford Pack would have supported her work and strengthened the Winthrop family’s position.","Marcus was Alpha Victor’s son, but Alpha Victor had never trusted him with the family’s research empire.","Serena was the grandchild he had groomed as his successor.","She had returned from four quiet years abroad and immediately dragged the Winthrop name into scandal.","Alpha Victor had been willing to give her everything she needed: money, contacts, influence, and a place in the family business.","She had traded all of it for Alpha Sebastian.","\"If this becomes public, what happens to my reputation?\" Alpha Victor demanded. \"If Eira takes this to court, what kind of future do you think you’ll have left?\"","Serena had heard enough.","The fear and guilt disappeared from her face. So did the innocent act.","\"If I stay with Sebastian and Eira forces us to repay everything, he won’t let us end up with nothing.\"","Alpha Victor went still.","\"Us?\"","The word hung between them."]},{"number":218,"title":"Chapter 218 Something to Wear for Fun","paragraphs":["\"What do you mean, ...us’?\" Alpha Victor’s brow furrowed. \"What does the Winthrop family need from Sebastian Hale? Does that arrogant CEO think he can buy his way into this family?\"","Serena let out a quiet breath.","Thank God. He had missed what she meant.","Alpha Victor tapped the deadline on the legal notice.","\"Ten days. If that money isn’t returned, Eira’s attorney will take this to court. One hundred eighteen million dollars, Serena. Where do you think we’re going to find that kind of money?\"","Tears spilled down Serena’s cheeks. \"Grandfather, you’ve never spoken to me like this.\"","\"Crying won’t fix anything.\" For the first time in her life, Alpha Victor did not soften. \"And don’t think you can wash your hands of this. The notice was served on Sebastian too. The money came from his marriage, but you were the one who received it.\"","\"So I’m not the only person responsible.\"","\"That is not the good news you think it is.\"","He set the notice on his desk.","\"You and Sebastian are meeting with Eira tomorrow. You’re going to settle this before it ever reaches a courtroom.\"","Serena’s lips parted.","A settlement was not the problem. She could not cover even half the amount, no matter what she sold. Was there really no way to make Alpha Sebastian pay the whole thing? She was carrying his child, for God’s sake.","\"Grandfather...\"","\"Tomorrow.\" His tone left no room for argument. \"And if you can’t handle something this serious, don’t call yourself my granddaughter again.\"","The words hit her like ice water.","Without Alpha Victor’s name behind her, Serena was nobody. Just another pretty face waiting to be used, discarded, and replaced the moment she stopped being useful.","\"I’ll go,\" she said quickly. \"First thing tomorrow.\"","Agree now. Find a way out later.","She wiped her cheeks and glanced toward the door.","\"It’s late. I should go home.\"","She needed to leave before anyone noticed how hard it was becoming to hide her pregnancy.","\"You’re staying here tonight.\"","Alpha Victor did not move.","\"The driver will take you to Eira in the morning. I don’t care what you have to do to get her to agree. Apologize. Beg if you have to. Just keep this out of court.\"","\"Beg her?\" Serena’s stomach twisted. The idea of begging Eira was humiliating.","Alpha Victor saw the defiance in her face, and his expression turned cold.","\"If this goes to trial, I’ll start over with someone else.\"","Serena stared at him.","The meaning was clear. He would cut her off. No more money. No more favors. No more carefully arranged opportunities.","\"Grandfather!\"","\"Your choice.\"","Alpha Victor walked out, leaving Serena alone in the study with the legal notice and the deadline hanging over her.","--","Meanwhile, Alpha Killian stepped off the plane and checked his phone. A string of messages from Natalie was waiting.","[Alpha, it’s Dr. Crawford’s birthday. You land at 10:10. Less than two hours until midnight. Better move.]","Option A: Money.","Option B: Yourself.","Option C: Money and yourself.","Alpha Killian’s silver-gray eyes paused on the words Eira’s birthday.","\"It’s Eira’s birthday,\" he said to Kate as they walked through the private terminal. \"I have less than two hours left.\"","Kate understood the assignment at once. Alpha Killian wanted to surprise Eira, and he wanted to do it tonight.","\"With your resources, you could have almost anything delivered within the hour,\" she said. \"But money probably isn’t the issue. The wrong gift could make her uncomfortable.\"","Alpha Killian slowed and glanced at her. \"Go on.\"","\"Whatever you give her will mean more if you choose it yourself.\" Kate paused. \"If you need an example of what not to do, look at Sebastian Hale.\"","The advice echoed something his mother had told him once.","Alpha Killian gave a quiet hum. By then, an idea had already begun to take shape.","Miles was waiting outside the VIP terminal with the car door open.","\"Southridge. Number Nine,\" Alpha Killian said.","\"Got it.\"","As they pulled away from the airfield, Alpha Killian glanced at him. \"How was Eira’s night?\"","Miles had not attended the reception, but Natalie had given him the full rundown during the drive. He knew Alpha Killian would ask.","He walked Alpha Killian through the night’s highlights, from Alpha Sebastian’s over-the-top husband act to Eira turning every move back on him and walking away with the crowd on her side.","Alpha Killian’s smile deepened.","Eira had finally shown Alpha Sebastian her teeth, and she had avoided every trap he set for her.","The car pulled up outside Southridge. Rain tapped against the windshield, shining beneath the porch lights. Alpha Killian stepped out without waiting for an umbrella and headed for the front door.","It stood slightly open.","He knocked once.","\"That must be him,\" Mrs. Jones called from inside.","\"My brother’s here,\" Lila added.","Alpha Killian pushed the door open.","Everyone turned, including the two dogs stretched out on the rug.","Eira looked over her shoulder. A smear of blueberry frosting marked one cheek.","The moment Alpha Killian came closer, she felt the chill clinging to him from outside. Raindrops still glistened in his dark hair.","She picked up the plate with the last slice of cake and held it out to him.","\"Yours, Killian.\"","His silver-gray eyes settled on the cake. \"You saved me a piece?\"","She nodded.","\"I cut it into four slices the second she started serving it,\" Mrs. Jones said. \"That one’s been waiting for you.\"","Lila nodded from across the table. \"She guarded it like her life depended on it.\"","Alpha Killian took the plate. Then he ran one finger through the frosting and touched it to the tip of Eira’s nose.","She blinked at him.","\"Happy birthday.\"","Before she could wipe away the frosting, Alpha Killian pulled a fine antique-gold chain from his pocket.","A single wolf fang hung from it, polished smooth with age, its base wrapped in aged gold. A tiny dark-red stone was set into the gold. Beneath the stone, fine lines had been worked into the metal, forming a small emblem that was easy to mistake for decoration.","\"It’s old,\" Alpha Killian said. \"I thought you might like it.\"","Eira turned the pendant over in her fingers. She had never seen anything quite like it.","Lila leaned closer, narrowing her eyes at the metal.[Wait. Is that the Sterling Pack’s crest?]"]},{"number":219,"title":"Chapter 219 The Fang","paragraphs":["Alpha Killian caught the faint skepticism in his sister’s expression and gave her a cool look.","Lila immediately backed down. \"Okay, okay. It’s a nice necklace. A little understated, maybe, but I guess that’s the point.\"","She glanced at the fang, then quickly looked away.","\"Don’t give me that look,\" she added. \"I’m just saying, if you were trying to impress her, you could’ve gone with something a little less subtle.\"","Alpha Killian’s eyes narrowed.","Lila lifted both hands. \"What? It’s pretty. It suits her. I’m done.\"","She turned to Eira with an innocent smile. \"See? Very understated. Very mysterious. Completely on brand for your terrifying billionaire Alpha.\"","Eira ignored the last part and studied the pendant in her palm. She turned the chain over, then tried to fasten the tiny clasp herself.","The clasp slipped between her fingers.","Alpha Killian noticed. \"Here.\"","Eira glanced at him, then handed him the chain.","Alpha Killian stepped behind her and gently moved her hair over one shoulder so he could reach the clasp. His fingers brushed the back of her neck as he fastened it.","Eira held still, suddenly aware of how close he was.","\"There,\" he said.","He let her hair fall back into place. The fang settled against her sweater, just below her collarbone.","Eira touched it lightly. \"How does it look?\"","Alpha Killian’s gaze rested on the pendant, then lifted to her face.","\"It looks good on you.\"","His tone was simple and matter-of-fact, which somehow made the compliment feel more personal.","\"Thank you,\" Eira said.","He gave a quiet hum and returned to his slice of cake.","\"Let’s eat,\" Eira said, nodding toward Mrs. Jones. \"Dinner’s probably getting cold.\"","Mrs. Jones began bringing the food to the table.","Alpha Killian looked up. \"You haven’t eaten yet?\"","\"Dinner was ready around the time you landed.\"","\"See?\" Lila said. \"Eira waited for you, and I’ve been sitting here starving.\"","\"You ate cake,\" Alpha Killian said flatly.","\"That was hours ago,\" Lila protested. \"Cake isn’t dinner.\"","Mrs. Jones brought out bowls of chicken soup, roasted vegetables, and pasta, putting an end to the siblings’ teasing.","The four of them settled around the table, the earlier teasing giving way to the easy quiet of a family dinner.","When Eira leaned forward, the wolf fang swung lightly against her sweater. Killian’s gaze followed the movement, and a faint smile touched his mouth.","Before she could reach for the ladle, he filled her bowl with soup.","\"Eat.\"","Eira picked up her spoon, then glanced toward the tall dining room windows.","Rain streaked down the glass, blurring the garden lights into soft, golden smears. The storm had washed the roads clean, leaving the yard dark and shining.","\"I have to leave for the airport tomorrow afternoon,\" she said. \"Hopefully the roads won’t be this bad by then.\"","\"Let’s hope so,\" Lila said. \"I’m not spending all night at the lab because the roads turn into a mess.\"","Alpha Killian looked at Eira. \"You’re leaving tomorrow to look for Sam?\"","\"Yes. Miles said I should clear it with you first.\"","\"Have Natalie book the flight through the office as a business trip,\" Alpha Killian said. \"Keep the destination off the regular itinerary. She can loop Vanessa in and limit access to the details.\"","If Alpha Sebastian found out Eira was returning to the Omega home, he would put people on every gate. That would make her search much harder.","Alpha Killian handled the problem in three sentences. No argument. No unnecessary questions.","He had seen the risk before it became a problem.","\"What time is your flight?\" Alpha Killian asked.","\"Afternoon or evening. I’m having lunch at my mentor’s wife’s place first.\"","He nodded and let the subject drop. Then he reached for the breadbasket and nudged it toward her.","\"Have some of that too.\"","Eira looked at him. \"I’m eating.\"","\"Not enough.\"","\"I’ve barely touched my soup.\"","\"You’ve barely touched anything.\"","Lila glanced between them, her smile growing. \"Should I leave you two alone?\"","\"No,\" Alpha Killianand Eira said at the same time.","They looked at each other.","For a second, neither of them spoke. Then Eira lowered her eyes to her bowl, while Alpha Killiancalmly picked up his spoon.","Lila bit back a laugh and focused on her dinner.","To anyone else, Alpha Killianand Eira might have seemed distant and impossible to read. Lila thought they were operating on the same wavelength, communicating through pauses, glances, and silences no one else could decode.","--","On his way home from a business dinner, Alpha Sebastian passed Number Nine. The warm light glowing through the tall windows made him slow down.","It looked like a family dinner.","Rain streaked the glass. Eira sat beside Alpha Killian, warming her hands around a bowl of soup and taking slow, careful bites. Someone was always checking on her, adding food to her plate or passing her a napkin before she had to ask.","Alpha Killian, obviously.","But not just Alpha Killian. His sister was there too, along with Mrs. Jones, the housekeeper Alpha Sebastian had hired to look after Eira.","Lila said something that made Eira laugh. It was an easy, unguarded laugh, the kind Alpha Sebastian had never managed to draw from her.","If he had been sitting beside her, he would never have treated her with Alpha Killian’s quiet patience. Isabella would not have made her laugh either. And his parents would not have shown up at all.","For four years, Eira’s birthday had been just the two of them. A grocery-store bouquet. A supermarket cake. Whatever dinner they could throw together after work.","He had never gotten a chance to make it five.","His eyes burned.","Alpha Sebastian stepped out of the car and stood in the rain, watching through the glass until the cold soaked through his coat.","He stayed there long after dinner ended and the others left the room.","He remembered the last time he had managed to get inside. Eira had been on the couch, with Alpha Killian’s arm around her waist as if it belonged there.","Alpha Sebastian’s hands slowly curled into fists.","He wanted to go in again. But the guard beneath the porch roof would spot him the moment he approached.","And Eira might not come out at all.He knew how much she hated him now.","The lights inside dimmed.","A few minutes later, Alpha Killian stepped out through the front door. He found Alpha Sebastian standing near the edge of the property, half-hidden in the darkness, soaked through and staring at the house.","Alpha Killian’s silver-gray eyes narrowed.","The guard approached with the dogs, but Alpha Killian lifted a hand.","\"Don’t wake her.\"","His gaze moved over Alpha Sebastian’s wet hair and rain-darkened coat. His voice was low and cold.","\"Well, look at that. You finally managed to let her eat dinner in peace.\"","He paused.","\"Enjoying the view, Hale?\"","The way Alpha Killian said his last name carried more weight than a direct insult.","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened.","\"You can throw your weight around all you want,\" he said. \"Eira will never choose you.\"","Alpha Killian said nothing.","\"She likes men who are gentle,\" Alpha Sebastian continued. \"Men with manners.\""]},{"number":220,"title":"Chapter 220 I’m Not You","paragraphs":["\"Once bitten, twice shy.\"","Alpha Killian turned his head slowly. A cold light flashed in his silver-gray eyes. The look he gave Alpha Sebastian was pure contempt, as if Alpha Sebastian were nothing more than something he had found crawling across his floor.","A faint smile touched his mouth.","\"Thanks for proving my point, Hale. You practically handed her to me.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened.","His hands curled into fists, his nails digging into his palms. After a moment, he forced them to relax and met Alpha Killian ’s stare.","\"And if you get what you want,\" Alpha Sebastian said, \"are you planning to marry her?\"","Alpha Killian’s faint smile disappeared.","\"I already told you. I’m not you, Hale. I don’t sleep with a woman and leave her without a ring on her finger.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s eyes hardened.","\"I never touched Eira before we were mated.\"","Alpha Killian looked him over, calm and completely unimpressed.","\"Who said I was talking about Eira?\"","Alpha Sebastian went still.","Alpha Killian meant Serena.","\"You’re finished with Eira, but you still haven’t claimed Serena. You’re going to let her carry your pup while you stand there and do nothing?\" Alpha Killian’s voice turned colder. \"Keep this up, and people are going to start calling you what you are.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s pupils narrowed.","\"A deadbeat father.\"","For a moment, the rain was the only sound between them.","They knew.","They knew Serena was pregnant.","\"How do you think we prepared the legal notice?\" Alpha Killian asked. \"We didn’t file it on a hunch. Your name and Serena’s are both tied to this mess. Neither of you is walking away clean.\"","Panic tightened in Alpha Sebastian’s chest, but he held on to his denial.","\"I have no idea what you’re talking about.\"","The contempt in Alpha Killian’s expression was impossible to miss now.","Alpha Sebastian knew there was no point in arguing. He would never win a battle of words against Alpha Killian, so he turned to leave.","The door opened behind him.","Eira hurried outside with a black umbrella in her hand and stopped in front of Alpha Killian.","\"You forgot this.\"","A moment later, she noticed the figure standing near the low garden wall.","Alpha Sebastian.","Her expression hardened.","Alpha Killian took the umbrella and opened it, angling it so the canopy covered them both.","Alpha Sebastian remained alone in the rain. Water had soaked through his coat, leaving dark patches across the fabric beneath the porch light.","\"Eira,\" he said quietly.","She didn’t spare him a glance. Her gaze settled on Alpha Killian instead.","\"Miles said the car had already left and that you were about to walk all the way back to Number One without an umbrella.\"","Alpha Killian’s brow furrowed.","Miles had dropped him off, but he would have called another car before letting Alpha Killian walk home through the rain.","So Eira had believed the first explanation she heard.","So this is how Alpha Sebastian kept her tied to him for four years, Alpha Killian thought.","It only took two people working together, and she never saw the lie coming.","She trusted people too easily.","Alpha Killian let out a quiet breath.","\"Eira,\" he said, \"don’t believe everything people tell you.\"","His gaze flicked briefly toward Alpha Sebastian before returning to her.","\"Remember that.\"","Eira opened her mouth to reply, but the sound of an approaching engine interrupted her.","A car pulled up in front of the house, its headlights washing over the driveway.","Alpha Killian glanced toward the car, then stepped back.","The driver lowered the window as soon as he stopped.","\"Sorry, Alpha. The rain made the roads slick, and I had to take it slow.\"","Alpha Killian gave him a cold look but said nothing. Instead, he took the umbrella from Eira and pressed it back into her hands.","\"Go inside.\"","The handle was still warm from his palm when her fingers closed around it.","Under his steady gaze, Eira turned toward the house. She never looked at Alpha Sebastian.","For a moment, Alpha Sebastian felt colder than the rain soaking through his coat.","Alpha Killian got into the back seat. He knew the guard, the dogs, and Mrs. Jones would keep Alpha Sebastian away from the house.","The car pulled away from the curb.","As soon as they were out of sight, Alpha Killian turned his attention to the driver.","\"You’re not new to this job. Checking the weather, planning for traffic, and allowing for delays are basic parts of it.\"","The slick roads had been an excuse.","The driver knew he had been caught. \"I’m sorry, Alpha. It won’t happen again.\"","\"Make sure it doesn’t.\" Alpha Killian watched him through the rearview mirror. \"Pass that along to Miles.\"","\"Yes, Alpha.\"","The driver’s stomach dropped. Alpha Killian knew about the umbrella stunt. He knew Miles had arranged it to bring him and Eira closer, and he knew the driver had played along.","--","Eira lay in bed with the lights off.","Outside her window, the world had faded into shades of gray. Weak morning light seeped through the curtains, but sleep still refused to come.","Part of her mind kept circling the problem of finding Sam. The rest kept drifting back to Alpha Killian.","Her fingers found the wolf fang resting against her chest. She traced its smooth surface slowly.","She had not told him, but she loved the necklace.","To Eira, the fang represented everything she had once wanted from a family.","When she was growing up, she had heard the other children talk about their fang pendants. In the Pack, a wolf fang was a protective gift, usually given to a young pup by their family. It was meant to keep them safe and remind them that they belonged somewhere.","Eira had wanted one more than she could explain. She had envied every classmate who wore one around their neck.","She had never believed she would receive one herself.","The thought stayed with her until sleep finally took over.","In her dream, she was back in her old classroom. Children crowded around their desks, showing off their fang pendants and comparing the different chains around their necks.","Her younger self sat quietly at the edge of the room, sketching a wolf fang in the margin of her textbook. The moment another child leaned over to look, she snapped the book shut and held it against her chest.","Even in the dream, she remembered how carefully she had guarded that tiny piece of hope.","Then a teacher called her name.","The teacher had never been part of the real memory.","Eira stepped into the hallway. Everything beyond the classroom had turned pale and hazy. At the end of the corridor stood a single figure.","Tall. Lean. Impossible to see clearly.","The figure reached out and held a fang pendant toward her.","The next morning, Eira woke with the pendant clenched in her fist.","She had held it against her skin all night. The metal was warm now.","She slipped the chain beneath her thermal shirt. Even against her skin, the fang no longer felt cold.","Her heart, however, was beating slightly out of rhythm."]},{"number":221,"title":"Chapter 221 The Uninvited Guest","paragraphs":["Across town, at the Winthrop estate, Serena was hurried toward a waiting SUV.","Alpha Victor stopped her at the front steps.","\"I made a few calls,\" he said. \"If Eira isn’t at Southridge, check Sterling Tower and then the Thorne residence. Find her and settle this quietly.\"","\"Grandfather, I can’t just show up at—\"","\"You can, and you will. Tell her we need time to gather the money. Apologize if you have to. Beg if you have to. Just keep this out of court.\"","Serena swallowed. \"Do you really think she’ll listen?\"","\"I don’t care what you think. Do you understand me?\"","She forced a nod. \"Yes.\"","\"Good. Go.\"","The driver dropped her at Southridge Estates a few minutes later.","Serena had visited the property with Isabella before, so security already had her name in the visitor database.","She gave the guard her name and told him she was there to visit the Hale residence at House Eleven.","After a quick check of the visitor list, he lifted the gate.","The moment she passed the gates, security notified Alpha Killian.","He called Mrs. Jones.","\"Keep her away from Eira.\"","Mrs. Jones understood.","Lila had been up since sunrise and was halfway through breakfast when barking broke the quiet morning. She set down her coffee and stepped onto the porch.","Serena was stuck in the middle of the driveway, with a German shepherd latched onto each of her knee-high leather boots.","The dogs weren’t hurting her, but they had no intention of letting her go.","She tried to pull one foot free.","The dog leaned back, tightening its grip.","\"Help!\" Serena cried. \"Get them off me!\"","Her driver rushed out of the SUV and moved toward her.","\"Stay back!\" one of the guards shouted as Serena’s driver reached for the metal rod. \"Don’t make any sudden moves.\"","The dogs held their ground.","Lila came down the porch steps in her slippers, a coffee mug in hand. She took a slow sip while Serena struggled to keep her balance.","\"Well, look who finally showed up,\" Lila said. \"A little late, though. The sun’s been up for hours.\"","\"Miss Sterling,\" Serena said through clenched teeth, \"call off your dogs. I need to speak with Eira. It’s important.\"","\"You can talk from there. They haven’t even broken skin.\"","\"I’m a guest.\"","\"A guest gets invited.\" Lila raised an eyebrow. \"You walked onto private property without permission. That makes you a trespasser.\"","Serena’s face flushed. She glanced at her driver, then lowered her voice.","\"Keep this up, and if something happens to my baby, you’ll be held responsible.\"","Lila stared at her.","\"Are you seriously using your pregnancy as a threat?\"","\"I’m warning you.\"","\"No. You’re trying to scare me into helping you.\" Lila set her mug on the porch railing. \"That’s not going to work.\"","Mrs. Jones stepped onto the porch beside her.","\"A moment ago, she was a trespasser,\" she said calmly. \"Now she’s threatening legal action over an unborn child. Her story keeps changing.\"","Lila nodded. \"Good point.\"","Serena’s breathing grew uneven.","Lila glanced at the dogs. If Serena fell or suffered a medical emergency on Sterling property, it could turn into a legal mess.","\"Duke. Scout. Let her go.\"","The dogs released Serena’s boots and stepped back.","Serena stumbled forward. Her expensive leather boots were covered in neat rows of puncture marks.","Lila tilted her head.","\"Honestly, they almost look intentional. Very edgy.\"","\"Enough,\" Serena snapped. \"I came here to see Eira.\"","\"To ask her to forget about the $118 million?\" Lila asked.","\"I came to ask for more time.\"","\"Then ask her attorney. Eira doesn’t owe you a private meeting.\"","\"Victor wants to speak with her.\"","\"Then have Victor call Susan’s firm.\"","Serena looked past Lila toward the house. \"I need to see Eira.\"","\"No, you need Eira to see you. There’s a difference.\"","Serena tightened her grip on her purse. \"You don’t understand what’s at stake.\"","\"Oh, I understand perfectly.\" Lila’s voice lost its playful edge. \"You accepted Sebastian’s money, cars, jewelry, and property. Now Eira wants it back, and everyone suddenly wants a quiet little conversation.\"","She picked up her coffee again.","\"Here’s my advice. Start selling things. The cars, the house, whatever you can unload. You’re going to need the money.\"","\"I never said we wouldn’t repay it,\" Serena snapped. \"But I need to talk to Eira. There’s no reason to turn a private matter into a public scandal. She’s an internationally respected researcher now. Why drag this into court and humiliate herself?\"","Lila gave her a slow round of applause.","\"How thoughtful of you. I’m sure you showed Sebastian the same courtesy.\"","Serena’s expression tightened.","\"But save the speech,\" Lila continued. \"Eira isn’t Sebastian, and she’s not going to fall for a sob story.\"","Her smile disappeared.","\"Now, are you leaving, or do I call the dogs back?\"","Serena found no opening. She turned and walked back to the SUV with what little dignity she had left.","Once they were on the road, the driver muttered, \"Eira probably isn’t even here. If she were, she wouldn’t be hiding behind all this security.\"","Serena stared out the window.","He might be right.","\"Sterling Tower,\" she said.","The SUV had barely stopped near the entrance when a line of security guards blocked her path.","The lead guard stepped forward.","\"Ms. Winthrop, you’re not permitted on the property.\"","There was no polite lie about her being a stranger or an unverified visitor. They knew exactly who she was.","This had Alpha Killian’s fingerprints all over it.","Serena had never understood his interest in Eira.","Killian Sterling had inherited one of the oldest and most powerful Packs on the continent before he was old enough to drink legally in some states. His territory stretched across three states, and every border patrol answered to him.","Yet he had chosen a divorced Omega with no wolf and no prestigious family name.","Serena had once wondered if it was some kind of twisted preference.","Now she understood something else. Alpha Killian had built a wall of protection around Eira, and Serena could not find a way through it.","But she had no other choice. If she wanted to get what she needed, she would have to go straight to Eira.","Then, a different idea came to her.","\"Then I’ll see Professor Davies.\"","\"Professor Davies doesn’t see uninvited visitors either.\"","Serena bit back a curse.","She returned to the SUV and waited in the back seat, keeping her eyes on the entrance to Sterling Tower.","She had no intention of leaving empty-handed, no matter how long she had to wait."]},{"number":222,"title":"Chapter 222 Running Out of Options","paragraphs":["Serena spent the morning waiting outside Sterling Tower, but no one came down to see her.","Frustrated, she had the driver take her to the Thorne residence. Security turned her away at the gate.","That was the last straw.","She called Alpha Victor.","\"You made this mess,\" he said. \"Now clean it up. I only care about results.\"","The call ended.","Serena clenched her jaw. Fine. If Eira refused to see her, she would go to Alpha Sebastian.","The driver took her to Hale Tower. The receptionist recognized her immediately. Serena had visited Alpha Sebastian countless times, and Beta Jordan had always come downstairs to escort her up without asking questions.","That old sense of privilege returned. She lifted her chin, put on a polite smile, and stepped into the elevator as if she still belonged there.","When the doors opened, Beta Jordan was waiting.","He did not look happy to see her.","Alpha Sebastian had been drowning in financial trouble for weeks, and Serena’s name was tied to every problem. Beta Jordan’s job was on the line if Alpha Sebastian went down.","He had no patience left for her.","\"Ms. Winthrop,\" he said, his voice cool. \"What brings you here?\"","His tone stayed professional, but the warning underneath was clear.","Serena ignored him and headed for Alpha Sebastian’s office.","\"Alpha Sebastian is in a meeting,\" Beta Jordan said, stepping in front of her. \"He can’t see you right now.\"","\"Then I’ll wait in his office.\"","She tried to move around him, but Beta Jordan blocked her again.","\"You need an appointment.\"","\"I’ve never needed one before.\"","\"That was before.\"","Serena’s polite smile faded.","Beta Jordan picked up the phone and called the front desk.","\"Who cleared Ms. Winthrop upstairs? From now on, no one goes up without an appointment and a confirmation call. No exceptions.\"","He paused, then added, \"Dr. Crawford is the only exception. She can come up whenever she wants.\"","Beta Jordan hung up and headed for the conference room.","Inside, Alpha Sebastian was wrapping up a video call with the Snowmark Group. They were finalizing the launch date for their joint project.","\"We’ve chosen a date,\" Alpha Sebastian said. \"If your team is ready, we can hold the launch tomorrow.\"","Soren hesitated. \"Tomorrow? Isn’t that cutting it a little close?\"","\"We’re ready on our end.\"","Soren had met Dr. Crawford the day before and was still impressed by her work. After a brief pause, he nodded.","\"All right. Tomorrow it is.\"","\"Then it’s settled, Soren. I’ll see you tomorrow.\"","The call ended.","Beta Jordan stepped into the room. \"Alpha, Ms. Winthrop is here.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s good mood vanished.","\"What does she want now?\"","\"She’s already in your office.\"","Alpha Sebastian gave him a sharp look.","Beta Jordan lowered his eyes. He had already dealt with the receptionist and knew he would be reviewing the new security rules with the entire front desk team. For now, he had no choice but to accept the blame.","Alpha Sebastian pushed open his office door.","Serena sat behind his desk as if she belonged there. An open velvet ring box rested on her lap. Inside lay Eira’s old mate-bond ring, its familiar design catching the light.","Alpha Sebastian’s expression changed the moment he saw it.","He crossed the room in three strides and snatched the box from her hands. Then he turned and handed it to Beta Jordan.","\"Put it somewhere safe.\"","Beta Jordan took the ring box without a word.","\"Sebastian,\" Serena said softly, \"you and Eira are over. Why are you still holding on to this?\" She placed a hand over her stomach. \"You should be thinking about us. About the baby. Don’t you want to hear our child call you Dad for the first time?\"","The mention of the baby softened him, if only slightly. His gaze dropped to her stomach.","\"I don’t need a reminder,\" he said. \"And keep your voice down. If you mess up the Snowmark deal, you know exactly what happens next.\"","Serena knew how to read him. She also knew when to use the baby to get what she wanted. If Alpha Sebastian lost the partnership, who would help her repay the $118 million?","\"Relax. I know what’s at stake.\"","\"If you do, why are you here?\" Whatever patience he had once shown her was gone.","Her eyes filled with tears. \"The demand letter. My grandfather tore into me over it. He told me to find Eira today and settle everything privately. But this affects both of us. I thought we should figure it out together.\"","Alpha Sebastian wanted the matter settled quietly too. If the legal notice became public, he would be the one taking the biggest hit.","\"Sell everything I gave you.\"","Serena’s stomach dropped. That was not what she had planned to hear. She had hoped to play the helpless pregnant woman and make Alpha Sebastian shoulder the entire debt.","\"If I sell everything, what happens to me and the baby?\"","\"If you don’t sell anything, there may not be a future left to worry about.\"","Serena fell silent.","\"But even if I start selling today, I can’t raise that much before the deadline,\" she said. \"We need to see Eira and work something out. Otherwise, we could both be served with court papers within ten days.\"","The thought made her chest tighten.","\"Eira isn’t taking this to court right away,\" Alpha Sebastian said.","Serena stared at him. \"What does that mean?\"","Had he managed to stop Eira? Did Eira still love him enough to walk away from more than a hundred million dollars? Serena could not imagine making a choice that foolish.","Alpha Sebastian had no intention of telling her how he had bought himself time.","\"Trust me. She isn’t moving forward with the lawsuit for now. But we still need the money ready in case she changes her mind.\"","\"How long is ...for now’?\"","\"Stop asking questions and do what I said.\" His patience was wearing thin. \"Sell the cars, the condo, and anything else you can turn into cash. We’ll deal with the rest later.\"","The moment Serena heard that Eira was not filing suit yet, the pressure in her chest eased.","She hated the thought of selling the cars and the condo, but she nodded. At least she had something to report to her grandfather.","Serena had planned to stay a while, act vulnerable, and use the baby to draw Alpha Sebastian closer. But he was already looking at the door, making it clear he wanted her gone.","She had no choice but to leave.","The moment she stepped outside, she called Alpha Victor.","\"Grandfather, Alpha Sebastian and I talked things over. Eira isn’t filing suit for now.\"","\"For how long?\" Alpha Victor’s voice was sharp. \"This is not a conversation we’re having over the phone. Come home. We’ll talk there.\"","He ended the call before she could answer.","Serena’s plan to return to her own apartment was gone.","If she went back to the Winthrop estate, Alpha Victor would soon realize she was pregnant. The relief she had felt only moments earlier disappeared, replaced by a tight knot in her chest."]},{"number":223,"title":"Chapter 223 Coming Home","paragraphs":["The Thorne Estate","By the time lunch was ready, Eira and Beatrice were already at the kitchen island, picking at a salad and arguing over whether the soup needed more salt.","The doorbell rang.","\"I’ll get it,\" Eira said.","A courier stood on the front step with a white bakery box tucked under one arm. Snow dusted the shoulders of his black jacket.","\"Eira Crawford?\"","\"Yes.\"","He handed her the box. A gold logo was stamped across the lid. Eira recognized it immediately. It was one of the bakeries in Sterling territory, the kind that usually required an advance order.","\"Someone’s feeling fancy,\" Beatrice called from the kitchen.","Eira brought the box inside and set it on the counter.","Beatrice glanced at the logo. \"That’s from Sterling.\"","\"Mrs. Jones ordered it.\"","\"Of course she did.\"","Eira looked at her.","Beatrice reached for another fork. \"What? She works for Killian. If she’s sending over a cake from that bakery, I’m guessing it didn’t come out of her own grocery budget.\"","Eira loosened the ribbon but did not open the box.","\"She said it was from her.\"","\"Sure.\"","\"Beatrice.\"","\"What?\" Beatrice smiled. \"I’m only saying the man has a very roundabout way of being thoughtful.\"","Eira’s fingers brushed the fang pendant at her throat.","\"He’s my friend.\"","\"I didn’t say he wasn’t.\"","\"You were about to.\"","\"I was about to say he seems to like taking care of you.\"","Eira looked away. \"You used to say Sebastian took care of me.\"","Beatrice’s smile disappeared.","\"Don’t mention that man while we’re eating. I just got my appetite back.\"","Eira laughed under her breath. \"Fair enough.\"","--","After lunch, Natalie texted Eira her travel details. Her flight left at four, and Natalie had booked her a hotel near the airport.","Eira replied that she would not need it. After landing, she still had a thirty-minute commuter-train ride and a cab ride to the orphanage. If everything went smoothly, she would arrive before dark.","Natalie had not realized how far the orphanage was from the airport.","I can book your train ticket too.","Thanks, but I already bought one.","After sharing another slice of cake with Beatrice, Eira returned to Number Nine to pack.","The moment Mrs. Jones heard where Eira was going, she went into full mother-hen mode.","\"Take a warm coat. Pack an extra sweater. Keep your phone charged, eat something before you leave, and call me when you arrive.\"","\"I promise.\"","\"And don’t skip dinner.\"","\"I won’t.\"","Mrs. Jones watched Eira zip her suitcase with the worried look of someone ready to climb into the car and come along herself. It took three promises before she finally let Eira leave.","Lila threw her arms around Eira.","\"Don’t go. Who’s going to keep my brother in line? He has nothing but sarcasm in that mouth of his. You’re the only person who can make him act human.\"","\"Does he know you talk about him like this?\"","\"He knows. He just pretends he doesn’t.\"","\"I have to go, or I’ll miss my flight.\"","\"Fine.\"","Lila released her and stood in the doorway, waving as Eira headed for the car. She looked so miserable that Mrs. Jones laughed.","\"Miss Lila, if Luna Seraphina and your father saw this performance, they’d feel terrible.\"","\"Please. Nothing gets to them.\" Lila rolled her eyes. \"Dad’s happiest when he and Mom are alone, acting like newlyweds twenty-four seven.\"","She paused.","\"Mrs. Jones, they’ve been married for years. How are they still this crazy about each other?\"","\"They weren’t always.\"","Lila turned. \"What do you mean?\"","\"Your parents had an arranged match. They married first and fell in love later.\"","Lila stared at her. \"Seriously?\"","Mrs. Jones nodded. \"Their story happened backward. Marriage first, love second, and a baby somewhere in between.\"","Lila’s mouth fell open.","\"How did I never hear this?\"","\"Some family stories are private.\"","\"That’s not an answer. What happened? Did they hate each other? Who made the first move? How old was Killian when my father finally claimed him?\"","Mrs. Jones sighed. \"Your father found Alpha Killian before he turned one. Alpha Killian has no memory of ever being the family surprise.\"","Lila blinked. \"Wait. My brother was an accident?\"","\"I said he was a surprise.\"","\"That is not better.\"","Lila burst out laughing and pulled out her phone. A moment later, she changed Alpha Killian’s contact name to:My Brother the Oops","--","The Airport","Eira had barely glanced at her ticket. She went straight to the regular check-in counter, only for the agent to smile and point her toward a private desk.","\"Ms. Crawford, first-class check-in is over there.\"","\"First class?\"","A few minutes later, Eira had checked in, cleared security through the priority lane, and settled into the first-class lounge. Natalie had even arranged a car to meet her at the airport.","She boarded before most of the other passengers and found herself in a wide leather seat with a full dinner menu in front of her.","She stared at it.","First class. Priority security. A car waiting at the other end. And a cake she had never asked for.","Suddenly, all the little details fell into place.","Natalie. Miles. Mrs. Jones.","They were not simply looking after her. They were quietly trying to push her and Alpha Killian together.","The flight attendant called her name, pulling her out of her thoughts. Eira ordered dinner, ate during the flight, and slept until the plane began its descent.","When the plane touched down, she collected her suitcase and followed the signs out of the terminal.","The moment she stepped outside, a blast of cold air hit her face.","The wind cut through her coat. Eira tightened her grip on her suitcase and looked toward the dark road beyond the airport.","Home was still hours away."]},{"number":224,"title":"Chapter 224 The Orphanage","paragraphs":["It was after nine when Eira finally reached the orphanage.","The old man at the gate did a double take.","\"Eira? What are you doing here? Gwen didn’t say you were coming. Come inside. I’ll call her.\"","\"It’s okay. I’ll go up myself. You stay inside where it’s warm.\"","He hesitated, but Eira gave him a reassuring smile before dragging her suitcase across the concrete. The wheels rattled through the quiet night.","A light flickered on in an upstairs window. A moment later, someone leaned out.","Eira looked up. \"Miss Gwen.\"","Gwen rubbed her eyes and squinted down at her. As soon as she recognized Eira, she disappeared from the window. A few minutes later, she hurried downstairs in a coat and slippers.","\"I heard that suitcase and thought someone had broken in,\" Gwen said. \"Why are you here so early? You should’ve called. Your hands must be freezing.\"","Before Eira could answer, Gwen opened her coat and tucked Eira’s hands against her sweater.","The familiar gesture took Eira straight back to childhood. She remembered squeezing into Gwen’s narrow bed, sleeping head to foot so she could tuck her freezing feet beneath Gwen’s arm.","\"I’m fine,\" Eira said. \"Come on. Let’s get you inside before you freeze.\"","She slipped an arm around Gwen and pulled her suitcase with the other hand.","The orphanage had changed a lot over the years. The children now slept in sturdy bunk beds with clean blankets, and Gwen finally had a small room of her own.","The Pack had also reinforced the doors and installed motion lights around the grounds. No one wanted another child disappearing from an unguarded shelter.","\"Take the top bunk tonight,\" Gwen said as they climbed the stairs. \"I’ll get one of the empty rooms ready for you tomorrow. We have two available now.\"","\"Okay.\"","\"Did you eat? Are you hungry? I can make you some noodles.\"","\"I ate on the plane. Don’t fuss over me. I just need to sleep.\"","\"All right. You must be wiped out.\"","Once Eira settled into the top bunk, she pulled out her phone and answered the messages waiting for her.","She let everyone know she had arrived safely, then shared her location with Beatrice and Martin.","After a moment’s hesitation, she sent it to Lila too.","Lila was thrilled to get the update before her brother did. She immediately went looking for Alpha Killian so she could tease him about it.","She had no intention of giving him Eira’s location without Eira’s permission. For now, her brother had officially dropped to the bottom of her priority list.","A message from Alpha Killian appeared on Eira’s phone.","Killian: You make it there okay?","Eira: I did.","Killian: Good. Get some sleep. Don’t worry about anything else tonight.","A moment later, another message came through.","Killian: If you need data support, contact Miles through the group chat. If you need legal help, call Susan.","Eira: They already have enough on their plates. I don’t want to keep leaning on them.","Killian: That’s what they’re paid to do. They’re not doing it for free.","Eira smiled faintly.","Eira: Miles isn’t on my payroll.","Alpha Killian stared at the message.","He typed, He’s on mine, then deleted it.","After a moment, he sent:","Killian: Handling client issues is part of his job.","The explanation sounded reasonable at first. The longer Eira thought about it, the less convincing it became.","She decided not to call him out.","Eira: Good night.","--","Before sunrise, Eira woke to the familiar sounds of the orphanage coming to life.","Miss Gwen was already downstairs, most likely helping prepare breakfast. Eira washed up, pulled on a warm sweater, and headed to the dining hall.","The younger children were lined up at the serving window with plastic trays in their hands. Breakfast was being served family-style, and the older kids had already left for school. The volunteers were checking lunch bags and making sure no child went outside without a coat.","One of the boys spotted Eira and shouted, \"Eira’s here!\"","Every head turned.","The little ones rushed toward her. In the middle of the crowd, a young girl lost her balance and fell. Her legs were weaker than the other children’s, and she could not keep up with them.","Eira hurried over, but two children reached the girl first. They helped her sit up, brushed the dust from her knees, and checked that she had not hurt herself.","\"You okay, Mia?\"","The girl nodded, embarrassed.","\"Go finish breakfast,\" one of the children told her. \"We’ll save you a seat.\"","\"Okay.\"","The children helped her back toward the line.","Miss Gwen came over with a bright smile and pulled Eira into a hug.","\"I could barely see you last night. Look at you now. You’ve filled out a little, and you look healthier than ever.\"","Eira laughed. \"That’s one way to welcome someone home.\"","\"I’m serious. Success looks good on you. Ever since your project took off, you’ve had this glow.\"","\"It’s not the success,\" Eira said. \"It’s the people around me. Being with the right people makes a difference.\"","Her gaze shifted toward the serving window.","A masked woman stood behind it, helping hand out breakfast. Eira did not recognize her. There seemed to be one more person working in the dining hall than when she had visited last year.","\"Is she new?\" Eira asked.","\"No. She’s a photographer. She’s filming a short video to help raise money for the orphanage and the children’s medical fund. She arrived a few days ago.\"","Eira looked at the woman again. The stranger kept her head down, but something about her posture felt familiar.","\"Where is she from?\"","\"Palo Alto,\" Gwen replied.","Eira’s eyes narrowed slightly.","\"Palo Alto?\"","Gwen lowered her voice. \"She’s staying near the clinic while she works. Her name is Crawford too, so just call her Ms. Crawford.\""]},{"number":225,"title":"Chapter 225 An Unexpected Face","paragraphs":["Eira never expected to find Lainey Crawford here.","Lainey seemed to feel her stare. She glanced up, offered a polite smile, and went back to spooning oatmeal into plastic trays.","This was not what Eira had pictured when she thought of the Crawford heiress.","The Crawfords had built their name in politics. Lainey had grown up hearing that public service meant staying close to ordinary people. Humility was part of the family brand.","Still, Eira could not help wondering whether this was more about good publicity than charity. A few well-edited videos of Lainey serving breakfast at a rural orphanage could do wonders for her image.","Eira turned to Gwen.","\"She checks out? Her paperwork too?\"","\"I looked into her myself,\" Gwen said. She knew exactly what Eira was worried about. A few years earlier, an influencer had staged an entire charity drive just to get more followers. \"Lainey’s legitimate. She provided references, identification, and proof of funding. The kids already adore her.\"","Gwen studied Eira’s face.","\"You two know each other?\"","\"We’ve met a few times, but we’re not close.\"","Eira had no idea when Lainey had come to this remote corner of Pack territory, or why she had chosen the very orphanage where Eira had grown up.","Lainey had always been polite. That was part of what bothered Eira. There was nothing obvious to point to, nothing she could call rude or suspicious.","Even so, something about the woman made the hair on Eira’s arms rise. Whenever Lainey’s eyes settled on her, a cold shiver ran down Eira’s spine.","Gwen followed her gaze toward the breakfast line.","\"She’s been helpful,\" she said. \"She even volunteered to help with the winter drive.\"","Before Eira could answer, Lainey walked over and pulled off her cap and mask.","\"Eira. We meet again.\"","\"Lainey.\"","The formal address told Eira enough. Lainey had done her homework.","They shook hands, then sat at one of the tables with their breakfast.","\"I never would have guessed this was where you grew up,\" Lainey said. \"Small world.\"","\"It is.\" Eira glanced at the camera equipment near the dining hall doors. \"Are you here to film your fundraiser?\"","\"I’m trying to. I haven’t shot much yet. The scenery out here is incredible, and the air is so clean.\" Lainey tilted her head. \"Aren’t you supposed to be buried in your research? How did you manage to come all the way home alone?\"","Eira’s eyes flicked toward Gwen.","Before she could answer, Gwen stepped in.","\"Her husband usually brings her here for Christmas.\"","Lainey gave Eira a long, knowing look.","\"Ah. That explains it.\"","Eira let out a quiet breath. At least Lainey had not mentioned Alpha Killian or the divorce.","But the truth could not stay hidden forever. Keeping quiet was not a solution. It was only buying time.","\"Miss Gwen, I need to talk to you later,\" Eira said. \"Privately.\"","Gwen’s expression softened. She understood at once.","\"I figured you did.\"","Outside, a patrol wolf crossed the edge of the property, checking the fence line before the next group of children went out to play. Eira watched him disappear into the snowy woods, then looked back at Lainey.","Something about this visit felt wrong.","--","The Office","Gwen locked the office door behind them and slid a folded sheet of paper across the desk.","\"When you showed up out of nowhere last night, I figured you were here about Sam.\" She tapped the paper. \"Take a picture, then hand it back.\"","Eira photographed the handwritten notes. Gwen folded the page and locked it in her desk drawer.","\"What happened to Sam?\"","She poured two mugs of herbal tea, added a pinch of dried honeysuckle to each, and handed one to Eira.","Eira wrapped both hands around the warm mug.","\"Sebastian tracked down Sam’s uncle and moved Sam to a new location. He also enrolled him in a new school. I don’t know which one.\"","Eira lowered her eyes to the tea.","\"He’s making sure I can’t find Sam.\"","\"To pressure you into what?\"","\"Pretending we’re still married,\" Eira said. \"We’re divorced now, but Sebastian used my name to close a business deal. He wants us to keep pretending we’re happily married whenever we’re in public. I refused, so he took Sam away to force me to cooperate.\"","Gwen reached across the desk and covered Eira’s hand.","\"He looked so charming,\" she said with a tired sigh. \"Turns out he’s just a coward in a nice suit. Why didn’t you tell me sooner? I could’ve helped you.\"","\"I didn’t want you to worry.\"","\"And now?\"","\"You said I looked better.\" Eira gave her a small smile. \"That’s enough. You can see for yourself that I’m okay.\"","Gwen sighed.","\"I still can’t tell if you’re strong or if you’re just used to handling everything by yourself.\"","Her expression turned serious.","\"You’re not going after Sam by yourself. You may have grown up here, but that doesn’t mean you know what everyone is capable of. I’d send someone with you, but traveling alone with a stranger is dangerous. Two women on the road by themselves is not much safer.\"","Gwen had always treated safety like a rule carved in stone. Every child who had lived under her roof knew to check the locks, stay in pairs, and call if plans changed.","\"Find someone you trust,\" she said. \"Otherwise, you’re not going anywhere.\"","Eira thought about it.","Alpha Killian was the only male friend she had, but he had a powerful Pack and a vast business empire to manage.","She could ask him to send someone, perhaps, but asking him to drop everything and come himself felt unreasonable.","But she didn’t want a stranger. She wanted someone she could trust.","\"I mean it,\" Gwen added. \"If you can’t find someone, I’ll go with you myself.\"","Eira glanced at her. Gwen was too important to the orphanage, and too old to be chasing leads across the country. The children needed her here.","Eira pulled out her phone and opened Alpha Killian’s messages. She typed a sentence, paused, and glanced down at the fang pendant beneath her sweater.","Then she pressed send.","Eira: Killian, I might need a favor.","His reply came almost immediately.","Killian: Name it.","Eira took a breath.","Eira: Come with me to find Sam.","The typing bubble appeared at once.","Killian: Send me the address.","Eira blinked.","That was it? No questions. No hesitation?","Before she could type another word, a second message appeared.","Killian: My consulting fee is eight hundred a day.","Eira stared at it for a second, then laughed.","The tightness in her chest eased. Of course he had to turn a personal favor into a business arrangement.","Eira: Fine. You’re hired.","Killian: Good.","A moment later, another message came through.","Killian: Miles is booking my flight now. Check your email.","Eira opened her inbox. A flight itinerary was already waiting for her.","Eira looked up from her phone.","\"Miss Gwen, I found someone.\"","\"Someone you trust?\"","\"Completely.\"","\"Good.\" Gwen stood and reached for the office door. \"Your room is ready. Let’s get your suitcase settled.\"","The room looked much the same as Eira remembered. The bunk beds were neatly made, and a few storage boxes had been stacked against the wall. Everything else was clean and orderly.","A framed photograph sat on top of one of the boxes.","Eira picked it up.","It showed her surrounded by the children during last year’s visit. Beneath it were older photographs from donor events, holiday parties, and Pack fundraisers.","She was in every one."]}]);
